Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an existential issue for us.\N这对我们来说是一个关乎存亡的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.60,0:00:05.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could easily stop, but if we stop today, we lose.\N我们完全可以停下来，但如果今天停下来，我们就输了。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.17,0:00:10.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Functionality, capability, safety, security, they're all at exactly the same place.\N功能、能力、安全与安保，全都处在完全相同的位置。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.11,0:00:20.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Priority number one.\N优先级第一。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.00,0:00:22.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's our third pod back together.\N这是我们第三次一起录播客。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.88,0:00:23.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yep.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.36,0:00:28.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the last 10 days, you've been uh at the Xi state dinner at the White House.\N在过去的十天里，你曾出席白宫举行的习近平国宴。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.52,0:00:33.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you were at the White House uh summit where we did the accord on superintelligence.\N你还在白宫峰会上参与了超级智能协议的签署。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.22,0:00:37.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and just yesterday, you were there with your parents um when the president, you know,\N就在昨天，你和父母一起到场，当时总统……
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.68,0:00:41.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,presented you with a National Medal of Science. the only investor at the table.\N为你颁发了国家科学奖章。你是当时唯一在场的投资者。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.80,0:00:45.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I there You were the only investor at the table.\N你确实是当时唯一在场的投资者。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.24,0:00:47.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now that now that we reflected on it.\N现在我们回顾一下这件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.64,0:00:48.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.03,0:00:51.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, and tell me being there with your parents yesterday, right?\N嗯，而且告诉我，昨天和你父母在一起时，感觉怎么样？
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.76,0:00:56.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It struck me five out of the six people on stage were all born outside of the United States.\N我突然意识到，台上六个人中有五个都是在美国以外出生的。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.84,0:01:00.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um how did that feel?\N那种感觉如何？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.16,0:01:05.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh well, first of all, it's a great honor all by itself.\N嗯，首先，这本身就已经是一种极大的荣誉。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.14,0:01:09.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and it's a reflection of the the contribution that the company has made.\N这也反映了公司所做出的贡献。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.04,0:01:14.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and obviously obviously we created we invented a new computing model.\N而且显然，我们创造了、发明了一种全新的计算模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.92,0:01:18.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is probably the most pervasive computing model in the world today.\N这可能是当今世界上应用最广泛的计算模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.24,0:01:20.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's the only computing architecture that's in every cloud.\N它是唯一一种存在于每个云平台中的计算架构。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.58,0:01:21.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's in every computer company.\N它被每一家计算机公司所采用。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.80,0:01:24.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's used in every field of science.\N它被应用于每一个科学领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.60,0:01:25.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's used by gamers.\N它也被游戏玩家所使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.74,0:01:29.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's used by creators and builders and it's used by scientists.\N它被创作者和建造者使用，也被科学家使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.00,0:01:31.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it powers intelligence.\N嗯，它驱动着智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.60,0:01:32.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.16,0:01:36.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, just if you take a step step back and you look at what what the company has accomplished,\N我的意思是，如果你退后一步，看看公司所取得的成就，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.52,0:01:39.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, we started out building a graphics chip for gamers.\N我们最初是为游戏玩家开发图形芯片的。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.50,0:01:41.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm still proud of that, of course.\N当然，我为此感到自豪。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.85,0:01:48.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we've now shipped 1.67 billion units.\N如今我们已出货了16.7亿个单位。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.26,0:01:54.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's how many generations of I mean, I raised generations of scientists and kids and designers, you know.\N这意味着我们培养了整整一代科学家、孩子和设计师。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.36,0:02:03.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so I think the impact that and here we are you know, we're the infrastructure that powers the intelligence of society.\N所以我认为，我们带来的影响是深远的，而我们如今正是支撑社会智能的基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.28,0:02:08.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so it's a it's an incredibly proud moment for me to receive the award on behalf of the company.\N因此，代表公司接受这份奖项，对我来说是一个无比自豪的时刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.02,0:02:17.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now for my parents you know, I wanted them to go and and I gave them literally you know, 24 hours notice time and they don't travel that much.\N至于我的父母，我想让他们来，所以我只给了他们不到24小时的通知，他们平时很少旅行。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.30,0:02:20.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,They don't travel that much and my dad didn't even have a suit.\N他们很少旅行，我父亲甚至没有一套西装。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.80,0:02:21.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.52,0:02:23.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so he ran out and bought a suit.\N是的，他跑出去买了一套西装。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.72,0:02:26.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh He looked great.\N而且他看起来很棒。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.61,0:02:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They looked great.\N他们看起来都很棒。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.52,0:02:31.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it was a brand new suit and he showed up and I I didn't realize he was he had a suit.\N是的，是一套全新的西装，他出现时我都没意识到他穿了西装。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.61,0:02:33.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thought he was just going to wear some shirt.\N我还以为他只是随便穿件衬衫。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.96,0:02:36.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so he went out and bought a suit.\N于是他出去买了套西装。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.26,0:02:40.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um my my mom got a new dress you know, and and literally in 24 hours.\N嗯，我妈妈买了新裙子，你知道的， literally 24 小时内就搞定了。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.04,0:02:41.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是啊。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.92,0:02:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, I know how it works.\N哦，我知道是怎么回事。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.00,0:02:45.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh my gosh, it's incredible.\N哦天啊，太不可思议了。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.38,0:02:49.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I so we got them on a we chartered a plane for them, got them there.\N所以我们给他们包了一架飞机，把他们送到了那里。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.48,0:02:54.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so they were so happy to meet the president.\N所以他们非常高兴能见到总统。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.24,0:03:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and President Trump walked my mom because she has a hard time walking and the two of them were were walking off stage and he he held her.\N特朗普总统搀着我妈妈，因为她走路很吃力，两人一起走下舞台，他还扶着她。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.36,0:03:03.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.56,0:03:09.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And walked it walked her down the stage and they were just incredibly incredibly proud to meet her meet him.\N他扶着妈妈走下舞台，他们俩都为能见到她、见到他而感到无比自豪。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.70,0:03:12.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um uh but for them it's their American dream.\N对他们来说，这正是他们的美国梦。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.96,0:03:13.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know,\N你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.54,0:03:16.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,my dad I still remember I was I think I was like 5 years old or something\N我爸爸，我还记得，我当时大概五岁左右，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.00,0:03:21.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,like that and and uh he had just come back from the United States on a business trip.\N他刚从美国出差回来。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.64,0:03:25.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,He was he was working for an air conditioning company and he was living in Taiwan?\N他当时在一家空调公司工作，住在台湾。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.80,0:03:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were at the time we had just moved to Thailand.\N当时我们刚搬到泰国。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.16,0:03:28.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thailand.\N泰国。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.48,0:03:34.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um Oh no, no, we were just about to move to Thailand and um we were in Taiwan.\N噢不，不，我们正准备搬去泰国，当时还在台湾。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.60,0:03:39.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,He had come back and he was he was in the United States working for a company called Carrier.\N他回来了，当时正在一家名为开利的公司工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.80,0:03:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're an air conditioning company and uh he was here for training.\N那是一家空调公司，他当时在这里接受培训。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.52,0:03:48.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um I of all the places in the world they landed him in New York.\N而且，全世界那么多地方，他们偏偏把他安排到了纽约。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.28,0:03:48.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.64,0:03:54.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so here you can just imagine a kid in the late 20s, I guess mid late 20s.\N你可以想象，一个二十多岁中后期的年轻人。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.28,0:04:00.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh never been outside of Taiwan, goes to United States, New York City of all places.\N从未离开过台湾，突然来到美国，还是纽约市。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.76,0:04:03.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he saw the future of the future.\N他看到了未来的未来。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.12,0:04:05.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he came back, you know, mind-blown.\N他回来时，简直震惊了。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.68,0:04:09.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh all the things that he bought at the airport and brought it back, you know,\N他在机场买的所有东西，带回来的时候，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.92,0:04:16.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,it was a he bought he he brought chocolate, he brought you know that cheese that you have in a tube back in the old days?\N他买了巧克力，还买了那种老式管装的奶酪？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.24,0:04:17.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's kind of like white cheese.\N就像白色的奶酪。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.55,0:04:18.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Strange cheese.\N一种奇怪的奶酪。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.38,0:04:19.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,It comes in a tube.\N它是管装的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.62,0:04:20.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's great.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.36,0:04:26.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh he brought back all kinds of strange things and he said, "This is we should go there someday."\N然后他带回了很多奇怪的东西，还说：“我们 someday 应该去那里。”
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.56,0:04:37.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the first opportunity they had they sent my older brother and I to United States and and um you know, it was it was his dream.\N他们第一次有机会时，就把我哥哥和我送到了美国，那正是他的梦想。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.24,0:04:40.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't think many people realize that you came to the United States ahead of your parents.\N我觉得很少有人意识到，你是比父母先来到美国的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.92,0:04:41.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是啊。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.24,0:04:42.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.42,0:04:45.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and they joined a few years later.\N几年后他们才过来。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.18,0:04:52.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it just hit me like a ton of bricks that five out of the six people on that stage yesterday were born outside the United States.\N但突然间我意识到，昨天舞台上六个人中有五个是出生在美国以外的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.06,0:04:57.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,You and I have talked about the need for you know, with all the other stuff going on,\N你我之前谈过，尽管有其他各种事情在发生，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.18,0:05:02.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,a real strategy and an immigration policy policy that makes certain that we're still\N我们确实需要一个真正的战略和移民政策，确保我们仍然是
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.98,0:05:05.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,the place that all the great builders in the world want to come build.\N世界上所有伟大建造者都想来建设的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.00,0:05:07.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,This this is America's superpowers.\N这就是美国的超级实力。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.80,0:05:08.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.20,0:05:16.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um in a lot of ways the intellectual property creation capability of our nation is unlike anything else in the world.\N从很多方面来看，我们国家的知识产权创造能力是世界上独一无二的。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.85,0:05:18.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is we attract the world's best.\N原因在于我们吸引了全球最优秀的人才。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.96,0:05:19.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.40,0:05:24.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we are the place where they want to come and build their lives because of the opportunity it provides,\N你知道，美国是人们渴望前来建立自己人生的地方，因为这里提供了机遇，
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.80,0:05:33.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,the freedom that that she offers, the opportunity that it provides, the spirit of of invention and entrepreneurialism and of the can-do attitude.\N提供了自由，提供了创新与创业精神，以及那种“我能行”的积极态度。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.93,0:05:37.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, in the United States everything is is possible.\N你知道，在美国，一切皆有可能。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.52,0:05:38.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.20,0:05:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We start with of course it's possible.\N我们首先想到的是，这当然可能。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.08,0:05:41.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course we could do that.\N当然我们可以做到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.77,0:05:46.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Instead of instead of you know, I I do a lot of travel and of course you can't do that.\N而不是像你那样，我经常出差，当然你做不到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.56,0:05:49.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course you know, In other places. in other in other places.\N当然，你明白的，在其他地方，在其他地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.33,0:05:50.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we take it for granted.\N我们习以为常。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.00,0:05:51.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,It does.\N确实如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.40,0:06:00.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the spirit, the the the energy um that comes around with the culture that we've created here, Yeah. um it's just can't be understated.\N但那种精神，那种围绕我们在这里创造的文化而产生的能量，嗯，真的无法被低估。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.90,0:06:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so I think the flow, the inflow of intellectual property into this into this country is unlike anything else the world's ever seen.\N所以我认为，智力资产流入这个国家的流动，是世界上前所未有的。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.28,0:06:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's true.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.76,0:06:12.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we want that.\N我们想要这种状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.68,0:06:19.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want all of the world's great minds to come here, bring their great ideas, you know, make them realize them here, Right.\N我们希望全世界的顶尖人才都来到这里，带来他们的伟大想法，让这些想法在这里实现，对吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.16,0:06:24.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,realize them here and let us, you know, let us let us keep that flywheel going.\N让它们在这里实现，让我们继续推动这个飞轮运转。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.33,0:06:27.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, I really it's a it's a delicate system.\N你知道，这确实是一个精妙的系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.32,0:06:28.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a delicate balance.\N这是一种微妙的平衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.53,0:06:30.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,I get it's a delicate balance.\N我明白，这是一种微妙的平衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.19,0:06:32.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,I get and so we have to do it lawfully.\N我明白，所以我们必须依法行事。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.10,0:06:33.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to do it rightfully.\N你必须正当行事。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.92,0:06:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but we we surely want to do it.\N嗯，但我们确实想这么做。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.64,0:06:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, for sure.\N没错，当然。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.48,0:06:39.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I want to start high level just kind of where we are.\N所以我想先从宏观层面开始，大致说说我们目前所处的位置。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.31,0:06:45.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then I want to dig down a little bit into the safety and regulation and getting this right.\N然后我想深入探讨一下安全与监管，以及如何把这件事做对。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.11,0:06:47.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where we are in terms of the compute build out.\N我们在计算能力部署方面目前处于什么位置。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.53,0:06:53.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then finally we're going to finish up you know, drilling in a little bit to Nvidia's growth and and and and what's going on there.\N最后，我们将进一步深入，探讨英伟达的增长情况以及当前的动态。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.84,0:06:56.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you've been really good at calling the future, right?\N但你一直很擅长预判未来，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.69,0:07:02.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Two years ago we were sitting here and you said that the market was dramatically underestimating the amount of compute\N两年前我们坐在这里时，你说市场严重低估了未来五年所需计算能力的部署规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.80,0:07:07.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,build out that was going to be required and was going to happen over the course of the next 5 years.\N也就是未来五年内需要完成、并且将会发生的建设规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.55,0:07:13.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,You You said it's not going to be a trillion, it's going to be 2 trillion at a minimum in terms of cumulative compute build out.\N你说过，累计计算能力的部署规模不会是万亿，至少会达到两万亿。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.21,0:07:14.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And of course now we're over that.\N当然，现在我们已经度过了那个阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.96,0:07:18.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,You said before everybody was thinking about it that inference, right?\N你之前说过，大家当时都在思考推理，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.35,0:07:23.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compute was going to 1 billion X because of inference time reasoning and thinking.\N计算能力将因推理时间而达到10亿倍，这是由于推理和思考的需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.28,0:07:30.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then last year of course, before we saw Opus 4.6, before we saw Claude code, you said we're entering the age of agents, right?\N嗯，去年我们还没看到Opus 4.6和Claude Code之前，你曾说我们正进入智能体时代，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.91,0:07:34.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where we're going to unlock a lot of these capabilities.\N那时我们将解锁大量这些能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.21,0:07:37.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and of course we saw Opus 4.6 and Claude code really took off.\N嗯，当然我们看到了Opus 4.6和Claude Code真正爆发了。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.02,0:07:39.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So where are we now, right?\N那我们现在在哪里，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.72,0:07:43.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,We We Elon and Sam and And only three things that I said that came true.\N我们只有埃隆、萨姆，还有我之前说的三件事成真了。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.58,0:07:44.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's another 200.\N还有另外200个。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.63,0:07:46.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why don't you just keep on going?\N你为什么不继续说下去？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.44,0:07:49.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,That I just let that be the podcast.\N我就让这期播客就这样吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.28,0:07:56.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I just So So So our investor day in a couple weeks is on, you know, entering the singularity, this acceleration.\N所以我刚刚说，我们几周后的投资者日，就是关于进入奇点，这种加速。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.36,0:08:02.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have Elon and Sam and Demis all say, "Hey, we're in the foothills or entering the singularity."\N我们有埃隆、萨姆和德米斯都表示：“嘿，我们正处于奇点的山脚，或正进入奇点。”
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.96,0:08:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have, you know, model solving Navier-Stokes, as you know.\N比如说，模型正在求解纳维-斯托克斯方程，这你也是知道的。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.04,0:08:11.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so when you look into your crystal ball, where are we?\N那么当你凝视水晶球时，我们目前处于什么位置？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.18,0:08:12.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And are we inflecting?\N我们是否正在发生转折？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.73,0:08:19.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are we accelerating, you know, into a different phase of superintelligence?\N我们是否正在加速，进入超级智能的新阶段？
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.04,0:08:23.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um And so let let's unpack that.\N那么，让我们来拆解一下这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.73,0:08:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,First First of all,\N首先，第一点，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.24,0:08:33.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's very fairly logical why the amount of compute that we're going to need is a billion times more than where we were just recently,\N为什么我们所需的算力将比最近（比如去年）高出十亿倍，这其实非常合乎逻辑，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.52,0:08:34.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,let's say call it last year.\N也就是说，去年的水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.82,0:08:42.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because thinking and problem solving takes a lot more,\N原因在于，思考和解决问题需要的推理远多于重复或背诵记忆的内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.20,0:08:49.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, inferences than repeating something, regurgitating something that you memorized.\N你想想，当你使用 ChatGPT 时，它接收到一个提示，其中大部分知识都已编码在大型语言模型中。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.53,0:08:57.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you're a ChatGPT, you give it a prompt, most of that most of that knowledge was encoded into the large language model.\N所以当你使用 ChatGPT 时，它接收到一个提示，其中大部分知识都已编码在大型语言模型中。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.76,0:09:00.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, of course, it hallucinated.\N不幸的是，它产生了幻觉。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.90,0:09:09.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the next click was it was it was a generative, but it was also grounded or conditioned by ground truth.\N所以下一步点击时，它生成的内容是基于生成的，但也受到真实信息的约束或条件限制。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.28,0:09:10.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.76,0:09:14.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,It would have to go out and do a search, do a quick search, comes back with the ground truth,\N它需要出去搜索，快速搜索一遍，然后返回真实信息，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.34,0:09:19.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then from that conditioning augment it with his own own what it already learned,\N再基于这些真实信息，结合它已有的知识进行补充，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.92,0:09:24.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,pre-training, and it would generate new new whatever the answer is.\N也就是预训练阶段学到的内容，然后生成新的答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.71,0:09:31.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, most of most of the things that we want to really do that are that are interesting requires you to to to reason step by step,\N事实上，我们真正感兴趣并想完成的大多数事情，都需要你一步步进行推理，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.57,0:09:34.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,to come up with several options, plan,\N提出多个选项，制定计划，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.21,0:09:35.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you might decide,\N你可能会决定，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.50,0:09:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,"Let's see how these things all roll out and then based on based on the answers of all of those I reflect on the best answers so far,\N“看看这些选项最终会如何发展，然后根据所有这些回答，反思目前最好的答案，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.52,0:09:44.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,the best path so far.\N目前最好的路径。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.81,0:09:48.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I might choose one or two or three of them, roll them out.\N我可能会选择其中一到三个，继续推进。”
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.28,0:09:48.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.60,0:09:50.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, prune the rest of it.\N好，把剩下的都修剪掉。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.11,0:09:51.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then just keep on doing this.\N然后就这样持续下去。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.47,0:09:59.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know, people we do this that's the reason why why we say um, great strategists love strategic optionality.\N你知道，我们之所以这么做，正是因为我们常说，优秀的战略家都重视战略灵活性。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.20,0:10:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You don't want to prune things too fast on the one hand, but you you also have to optimize your resources.\N一方面你不想修剪得太快，但另一方面你也必须优化资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.92,0:10:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, AI's are doing that.\N好，AI 正在这么做。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.80,0:10:11.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so so they're they're keeping their strategic optionality, they're rolling things out,\N好，它们保持着战略灵活性，持续推出新功能，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.60,0:10:16.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're pruning, um, they're they're reflecting, they're pruning, so on and so forth.\N同时也在修剪、反思、再修剪，如此循环往复。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.15,0:10:21.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And all of that thinking all of that exploration just takes a lot more compute.\N而所有这些思考和探索，都需要更多的计算资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.15,0:10:27.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and not on top of that, because it's able to now do productive things, we're going to use it for more things.\N而且不仅如此，因为现在它能做有产出的事了，我们就会用它做更多事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.67,0:10:31.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the compounding of both it uses more compute to do its job,\N于是，它不仅需要更多算力来完成工作，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.49,0:10:35.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it's doing a good job and therefore we're going to we're going to hire it to do more jobs.\N而且它干得不错，所以我们还会雇它做更多工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.32,0:10:35.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.00,0:10:36.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好，明白了？
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.36,0:10:37.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that all compounds.\N因此，所有化合物。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.98,0:10:38.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,\N嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.22,0:10:44.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,at this point I would I would say that the big observation from last year is that that on the\N此时我想说，去年最大的观察结果是，这一点上
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.72,0:10:48.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,one hand we want the models to get better and better and we we still want the models to get better.\N一方面，我们希望模型越来越优秀，我们仍然希望模型持续进步。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.29,0:10:51.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the scaling laws of models are are going to continue.\N模型的缩放定律将继续发挥作用。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.82,0:10:59.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, the attachment of a harness, basically the exoskeleton of the large language model.\N然而，为大型语言模型配备一个 harness，本质上就是为其构建一个外骨骼。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.32,0:10:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.80,0:11:07.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, kind of the body of the brain that allows it to um, manage manage working memory, manage knowledge.\N你知道，就像大脑中负责管理工作记忆和知识的那部分结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.51,0:11:14.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you go from working memory to short term, to long term, to basically formulating your knowledge graph, which is what we all do.\N你是如何从工作记忆，过渡到短期记忆，再到长期记忆，\N最终构建出自己的知识图谱的，这正是我们每个人都在做的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.03,0:11:21.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,We kind of think about, "Hey, you know, what did I learn and how does it fit into everything that I know in the past?"\N我们常常会想：“嘿，我学到了什么？它如何与我过去所知的一切相契合？”
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.30,0:11:24.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know how when we we go to bed, we do compaction.\N而你知道，当我们上床睡觉时，大脑会进行信息压缩。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.45,0:11:29.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Things that don't make sense, we kind of or don't matter, we kind of eventually forget.\N那些没有意义或不重要的事情，我们最终会渐渐忘记。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.48,0:11:32.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the things that kind of matter somehow it gets reconnected.\N但那些真正重要的事情，却会以某种方式重新连接起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.17,0:11:34.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we're doing that kind of offline.\N所以我们是在这种离线状态下进行的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.34,0:11:40.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we got working memory, we have offline knowledge extraction and creation, knowledge graph creation.\N因此我们拥有工作记忆，具备离线的知识提取与创造，以及知识图谱的构建能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.04,0:11:43.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um that whole part of memory is a big deal.\N记忆的这一整块区域非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.56,0:11:45.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other thing is, of course, tool use.\N另一个关键点当然是工具使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.92,0:11:46.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.16,0:11:53.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we we've taught these tools, these uh AIs, how to interact with uh the most important tools that the hum- humans ever made.\N我们已经教会这些工具，这些AI，如何与人类历史上最重要的工具进行交互。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.29,0:11:58.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, it's no different than uh if you were if you were a robot comes into our house,\N就像如果你是一台机器人进入我们的家，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.62,0:12:03.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh it's more likely you're going to use all the tools that I have in the house than to go off and build it from scratch.\N你更可能使用我家里已有的所有工具，而不是自己从头开始去制造。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.85,0:12:10.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so uh so SPICE is still going to be useful and um Verilog will be useful and uh simulators will be useful and you know,\N所以SPICE仍然有用，Verilog仍然有用，仿真器也仍然有用，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.77,0:12:18.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,design compilers and and and you know, Photoshop and AutoCAD and you know, the CATIA and all the Siemens tools.\N设计编译器，还有你知道的 Photoshop 和 AutoCAD，\N以及 CATIA 和西门子的所有工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.72,0:12:22.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these different tools that we've been using to run our company, build our company,\N我们用来运营公司、构建公司的所有这些不同工具，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.34,0:12:26.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,design things, operate things, they're all going to be great tools for the agents to use.\N无论是设计东西还是操作东西，都将成为智能体使用的绝佳工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.37,0:12:29.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the agents had to learn how to use it.\N但智能体必须学会如何使用这些工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.19,0:12:39.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so these two areas knowledge, knowledge um and working memory and um tool use, huge unlocks in the last year.\N于是过去一年里，这两个领域——知识、工作记忆，以及工具使用——取得了巨大突破。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.32,0:12:39.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.60,0:12:44.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now all of the sudden you could you could put these large language models\N所以现在突然之间，你可以把这些大型语言模型
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.46,0:12:51.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,encapsulated in their um harness or exoskeleton and you can put them into your company,\N封装在它们的运行框架或外骨骼中，然后将它们引入你的公司，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.80,0:12:56.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,connect them to uh the the information, the ground truth that you have,\N将它们连接到你拥有的信息和真实数据，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.40,0:13:00.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,connect them to the the tools that they can use, and all of a sudden they start doing amazing things.\N连接到它们可以使用的工具，突然之间，它们就开始展现出惊人的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.89,0:13:04.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now the the easiest part uh frankly was coding.\N现在，最简单的部分——坦白说——是编程。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.72,0:13:05.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.12,0:13:08.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's kind of the the the first on-ramp, you know, to useful work.\N这就像是通往实用工作的第一个入口，你知道的。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.94,0:13:10.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and in a lot of ways,\N而且在很多方面，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.48,0:13:15.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh coding is easy because both the customer and the work the the\N嗯，编程其实很简单，因为客户和他们使用的工具都对那些用途广泛，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.70,0:13:22.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,tools that they use are fairly accustomed to uh things that has tremendous use,\N但又不太容易使用的工具已经相当熟悉了。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.70,0:13:25.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,but are not extremely easy to use.\N但并不特别好用。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.26,0:13:31.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so in the early days of coding, it's it wasn't extremely easy to deploy, um but software engineers found a way.\N所以在编程的早期阶段，部署并不容易，不过软件工程师找到了办法。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.94,0:13:39.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so now now I think the next click for us is now uh and and you guys have probably been playing with Astra, OpenAI's Astra.\N所以现在，我认为我们接下来要做的就是——你们可能已\N经试用过 Astra，OpenAI 的 Astra。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.77,0:13:43.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's really fantastic, and we're using it in all these different places.\N它真的很棒，我们正在各个地方使用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.15,0:13:51.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, now the next the next phase of these these agents, they're able to do, you know, design work and a lot of creative marketing work,\N所以现在，这些智能体的下一个阶段，能够完成设计工作和大量创意营销工作，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.88,0:13:58.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we're using it to go you take a picture and give it to Astra, it literally recreates it into CAD.\N我们用它来做这样的事：你拍张照片交给 Astra，它会直接把它还原成 CAD 模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.84,0:13:59.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.32,0:13:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.80,0:14:01.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,It recreates it in the into the the CAD.\N它将模型重新创建到CAD中。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.96,0:14:05.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, which is incredible, because we need the CAD Yes.\N所以，这非常不可思议，因为我们需要CAD，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.28,0:14:09.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,so that we can we can interact with the CAD and make fine-tuning and adjust.\N这样我们才能与CAD交互，进行微调和调整。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.76,0:14:13.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, Astra could really give us the the first initial implementation.\N因此，Astra可以真正为我们提供最初的实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.54,0:14:15.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Incredibly productive.\N极其高效。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.12,0:14:23.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you take you take Astra and and but you know, the the latest release and you apply to all of these different different domains.\N你拿Astra，使用最新版本，应用到所有这些不同的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.24,0:14:30.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I I think that that besides software engineering, you know, we're going to see designers and builders and creators and you know,\N我认为，除了软件工程之外，我们还将看到设计师、建造者、创造者，以及……
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.19,0:14:34.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,this whole area, scientists, and you know, all of all of this whole unlocking.\N这整个领域，科学家们，以及所有这些被解锁的潜力。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.60,0:14:42.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, the challenge, of course, is how do we deploy agents safely and securely into the world's enterprise?\N现在，挑战当然是如何安全、可靠地将智能体部署到全球企业中？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.39,0:14:46.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is exactly the same question again with safety and security.\N这又回到了安全与安保这个完全相同的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.08,0:14:49.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and and and we'll talk about it. about it.\N嗯，我们稍后会讨论这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.30,0:14:50.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll we'll we'll come in on that.\N我们会就此展开讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.43,0:14:56.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,What what I'm what I'm struck by is that all of this occurred this year with OpenAI and Anthropic having,\N我感到震惊的是，这一切都发生在今年，而 OpenAI 和 Anthropic 每家拥有的算力不过，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.80,0:15:00.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know, two, three gigawatts of compute each, okay?\N我不知道，大约两到三吉瓦的算力，好吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.12,0:15:05.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, relatively small amount of compute relative to what's coming, okay?\N相对于即将到来的算力规模而言，这其实是非常小的量，好吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.20,0:15:06.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, again,\N所以，再次强调，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.40,0:15:16.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,what I'm interested in is the way the economy generally works or people model the economy or they model a company is linear deceleration.\N我感兴趣的是，经济通常是如何运作的，或者人们如何建模经济，\N或者他们如何建模一家公司，通常认为是线性减速。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.82,0:15:20.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're not very good at modeling acceleration.\N但他们并不擅长建模加速。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.64,0:15:22.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,But here we have this double exponential.\N但在这里，我们看到了双指数增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.57,0:15:26.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have massive amount of new compute coming on board.\N大量新的算力即将投入使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.20,0:15:32.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if OpenAI and Anthropic are, I don't know, three to five x'ing their compute next year, does it stand to reason?\N所以如果 OpenAI 和 Anthropic 明年算力提升三到五倍，这合理吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.78,0:15:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we solved Navier-Stokes.\N我的意思是，我们已经解决了纳维-斯托克斯方程。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.16,0:15:39.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll look back at this and say that was a tiny amount of compute and intelligence,\N我们回过头来看，会发现这其实只是非常少的算力和智能，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.66,0:15:44.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,the worst intelligence we're ever going to have from here forward, solving a a millennium problem.\N这是我们未来所能拥有的最差的智能，却解决了千年难题。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.04,0:15:51.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you look at what's coming online next year, you know, do you expect that we're going to have major breakthroughs in,\N所以当你展望明年即将上线的技术时，你是否预期我们将在这些长期存在\N的代理式问题上取得重大突破，从而能够运用大量智能体集群来解决它们？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.48,0:15:58.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, long-running agentic uh uh problems that that that we can use these swarms of agents on?\N你知道，我们能否利用这些智能体集群来解决长期存在的代理式问题？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.80,0:16:01.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, Navier-Stokes is is really a great example.\N好的，纳维-斯托克斯方程就是一个很好的例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.30,0:16:07.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um remember, uh OpenAI did not solve Navier-Stokes from nothing.\N嗯，记得，OpenAI 并不是从零开始解决纳维-斯托克斯方程的。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.12,0:16:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Correct.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.76,0:16:14.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,They solved it from the foundation of a lot of great scientists, a lot of great mathematicians, and a lot of great previous work.\N他们是基于众多杰出科学家、杰出数学家以及大量前期研究成果才完成的。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.36,0:16:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Earlier I said, we're at we're at kind of the tipping point of a lot of these different fields.\N之前我说过，我们正处于这些不同领域发展的临界点。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.24,0:16:20.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.64,0:16:28.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because we're kind of at that phase, that that point with Navier-Stokes, with a great deal of foundational work already been done.\N因为我们正处于这样一个阶段，就像纳维-斯托克斯方程一样，已经完成了大量基础性工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.39,0:16:34.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,If we could just apply the exhaustive exploration of AI Yes.\N如果我们能对以往的工作进行AI的全面探索，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.48,0:16:40.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the previous previous done work, we're going to see one breakthrough after another breakthrough rather quickly.\N我们将很快接连看到一个又一个突破。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.76,0:16:42.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we do need a lot of compute to do that.\N但我们也需要大量的算力来实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.02,0:16:46.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and and the reason for that is because a large amount of exploration was necessary.\N而且之所以如此，是因为需要进行大量的探索。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.90,0:16:56.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, if it was if it was simply somebody resolving some fundamental first principle theory in order to discover the breakthrough.\N你知道，如果只是有人解决了某个基本原理理论，从而发现突破性成果的话。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.32,0:17:03.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it didn't require a vast amount of exploration of space, uh search space, not space space, but search space.\N如果不需要对庞大的搜索空间进行广泛探索——不是物理空间，而是搜索空间。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.39,0:17:06.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,If it didn't require that, then somebody would have found it earlier.\N如果不需要这样，那么早就有人发现了。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.08,0:17:08.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right. people are pretty smart.\N没错，人们相当聪明。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.26,0:17:15.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so I I think that there are many problems like this that are just on a precipice,\N所以我认为，还有很多类似的问题正处在临界点上，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.24,0:17:21.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,and and really wants to just have that massive amount of intelligence exploration to to get us there.\N真正需要的是大规模智能探索，才能推动我们到达那里。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.32,0:17:27.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um In the In the coming years, you know,\N未来几年里，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.58,0:17:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,my expectation is is that the the cost of intelligence would fall fairly fairly quickly.\N我的预期是，智能的成本会迅速下降。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.36,0:17:36.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.24,0:17:40.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because obviously we're bringing more compute online.\N原因很明显，因为我们正在接入更多的计算资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.20,0:17:42.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um these models are getting smarter.\N这些模型正变得越来越聪明。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.80,0:17:44.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you're smarter, you could be more efficient.\N聪明程度越高，效率就可能越高。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.80,0:17:45.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.48,0:17:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the combination of these two things, the the cost of intelligence will come down, which is which is of course what they want.\N因此，这两者的结合将使智能成本下降，这当然是他们所希望的。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.72,0:17:52.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.00,0:17:53.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is no different than Moore's law.\N这和摩尔定律没什么不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.59,0:18:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you go back 30 somewhat years, we we have three decades of computing cost decreasing by a factor of two every single year.\N如果回溯到大约30年前，我们经历了三十年，计算成本每年下降一半。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.04,0:18:03.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.36,0:18:09.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and we want intelligence cost to decrease by a factor of two or 20 every single\N我们希望智能成本每年下降一半或20倍，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.41,0:18:14.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,year because we the consumption of it is going to It's going to more than up for it.\N因为我们对它的消耗将会大幅增加，足以弥补这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.32,0:18:14.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's Jevons paradox.\N这就是杰文斯悖论。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.92,0:18:15.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.40,0:18:16.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,More than make up for it.\N完全足以弥补这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.44,0:18:23.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so there's there's a massive empty space in the world that wants to be filled, empty vacuum of of of opportunity.\N世界上存在一个巨大的空白，一个渴望被填补的机遇真空。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.02,0:18:26.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And we just got to get get the cost down.\N我们只需把成本降下来。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.48,0:18:32.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I I guess what stands out to me about Navier-Stokes is that they had 10,000 agents working together.\N我觉得纳维-斯托克斯方程最突出的地方在于，它们有1万个智能体协同工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.44,0:18:40.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Almost looks like a To me that sounds like a you know, a hyper-scale company basically all pointing agents to work together towards a goal.\N对我来说，这看起来就像一家超大规模公司，基本上所有智能体都指向同一个目标协同工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.12,0:18:40.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N是这样吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.47,0:18:46.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think in the early days right now, it's a lot a lot of you know, paralyzed search exploration.\N我认为在早期阶段，目前还存在大量因僵化而停滞的探索。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.49,0:18:54.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think you know, the the goal is that more of these agents can work together to a common goal and that we can solve a lot more.\N但我觉得，这些智能体能更多地协同合作，朝着共同目标前进，我们就能解决更多问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.27,0:19:01.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to your point, you know, I think our math says probably cost about $4 million of compute to solve solve,\N就你提到的点，我认为我们的计算表明，解决这个纳维-斯托克斯实例的成本大概在400万美元左右。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.87,0:19:05.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, this instantiation of Navier-Stokes.\N也就是这个纳维-斯托克斯方程的实例。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.12,0:19:13.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the cost will the cost to do something like that over the next few years is going to drop by another 5x, 10x, right?\N未来几年内，完成类似任务的成本还将下降5倍、10倍，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.15,0:19:20.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the the number of things that we're going to be able to do is is rapidly expanding. going to go sky high.\N因此，我们能够完成的任务数量将迅速增加，呈指数级增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.88,0:19:28.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the original GPT probably cost, let's pick a number, say you know, maybe $20 to do.\N原始的GPT大概成本是，我们随便选个数字，比如可能20美元左右。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.24,0:19:32.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you wanted to train GPT-1 now, it'll probably cost you what?\N如果你现在想训练 GPT-1，大概需要多少钱？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.42,0:19:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,$1,000, $100, maybe?\N1000 美元，100 美元，也许吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.00,0:19:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like 100 bucks, yeah.\N大概就是 100 美元，没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.84,0:19:35.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.19,0:19:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you you went from you went from $20 or say $10 to 100 bucks.\N所以，你从原来的 20 美元，或者说 10 美元，涨到了 100 美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.20,0:19:43.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we did that in 10 years.\N而我们只用了 10 年就做到了这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.12,0:19:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.16,0:19:44.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.95,0:19:53.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I fully expect meanwhile uh our ambition got so large that the models that we're training now,\N所以，与此同时，我们的目标变得越来越大，我们现在训练的模型，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.69,0:19:58.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,3 trillion, 10 trillion, 30 trillion, we're talking about gigantic models now.\N3 万亿、10 万亿、30 万亿，我们现在谈的是巨型模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.84,0:20:03.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we want it to be and so our ambition for for the capabilities of technology has gone up.\N而且我们对技术能力的期望也提高了。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.74,0:20:09.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, our use of it has gone up between 10 years ago to now, probably I don't know, a million times.\N同时，我们对它的使用量从 10 年前到现在，可能增长了一百万倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.04,0:20:13.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I I don't think this trend is going to stop.\N所以我认为，这种趋势不会停止。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.14,0:20:19.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think this is there's a there's a fairly insatiable demand for for intelligence.\N我觉得人们对智能的需求是相当难以满足的。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.11,0:20:26.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the more the smarter you are, the the more intelligent you are, the more ideas of applying intelligence you have.\N你越聪明，越有智慧，就越能想到更多应用智能的点子。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.60,0:20:32.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, it's the more I've learned in life, the more I realize there's more to do.\N你知道，我越学习，就越意识到还有更多事情要做。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.77,0:20:36.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's because every single every time you learn something, it opens a new door.\N这是因为每当你学到了新东西，就会打开一扇新的门。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.16,0:20:37.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every time you learn something opens a new door.\N每当你学到新东西，就会打开一扇新的门。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.76,0:20:42.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And every time you open a new door, you see more opportunity, you see more challenges, see more problems.\N每当你打开一扇新门，就会看到更多机会、更多挑战，也看到更多问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.67,0:20:45.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, that's kind of that's the future.\N所以，这就是未来的模样。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.28,0:20:45.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.68,0:20:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, people say we're going to have more time.\N人们说我们会拥有更多时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.80,0:20:50.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I completely disagree.\N我完全不同意。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.16,0:20:55.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think I think for most people this intelligence is going to unlock more opportunities,\N我认为对大多数人来说，这种智能将解锁更多机会。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.06,0:20:57.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is going to and they're going to want to pursue it because they're ambitious.\N这将会成为他们的目标，因为他们有雄心壮志，所以会去追求。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.00,0:20:58.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.80,0:21:04.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, give me an example of a family, a father, a son, you know, a husband, a wife,\N举个例子，一个家庭，父亲、儿子，丈夫、妻子，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.31,0:21:09.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,a mother, who doesn't want it who who don't have ambition for their families to have more?\N母亲，谁不希望自己的家庭过得更好呢？谁没有对家庭的更高追求呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.85,0:21:13.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just They just don't have the opportunity and these things are going to open up opportunity.\N他们只是缺乏机会，而这些事情将打开新的机会之门。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.24,0:21:18.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you go back to 1930, Keynes talked He made a prediction about the Industrial Revolution.\N如果回到1930年，凯恩斯曾谈论过工业革命。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.29,0:21:24.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he said, you know, in 100 years the economy will have 8x, but the work week will go to 15 hours a week.\N他说，一百年后，经济将增长八倍，而每周工作时间将缩短至15小时。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.78,0:21:25.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,He was right.\N他猜对了。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.96,0:21:27.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,The economy did 8x, right?\N经济确实增长了八倍，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.04,0:21:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had massive abundance and productivity gains from it.\N我们从中获得了巨大的丰裕和生产率提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.92,0:21:32.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, except we're working 80 hours a week.\N是的，但我们现在每周工作80小时。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.16,0:21:34.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but we didn't go to a 15-hour week.\N但我们并没有进入每周15小时工作制。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.12,0:21:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what what he got wrong was the human spirit.\N而他错就错在低估了人类精神。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.36,0:21:38.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.73,0:21:41.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,He didn't realize that that work is purpose.\N他没意识到，工作本身就是目的。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.38,0:21:43.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Discovery is purpose, right?\N探索本身就是目的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.56,0:21:46.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's deeply encoded in I think our DNA.\N我认为这深深编码在我们的DNA里。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.28,0:21:49.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm working harder than I ever have, having more fun than I ever have.\N我现在比以往任何时候都更努力，也比以往任何时候都更快乐。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.91,0:21:53.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not because I have to, like my grandparents did, right?\N并不是因为像我祖父母那样不得不如此，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.58,0:21:55.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm doing it because I want to.\N我是出于自己的意愿在做这件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.08,0:21:55.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.48,0:21:58.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and so I I agree with you on that.\N嗯，所以我同意你的看法。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.13,0:22:03.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I I'm I'm fascinated with this idea, you know, the singularity postulates that, you know,\N我对这个想法着迷，你知道，奇点理论认为，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.40,0:22:09.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,we we've kind of now have all these agents that can work together on long-running tasks, they can stay on task.\N我们现在拥有了各种智能体，它们能协同完成长期任务，还能保持专注。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.99,0:22:13.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I love your Keep each other on task, working as a team.\N嗯，我喜欢你们互相督促、团队协作的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.37,0:22:14.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey, you're off.\N嘿，你被罚下了。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.20,0:22:14.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.83,0:22:19.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,I love your idea that, you know, we build on on top of all the things that have come, right?\N我很喜欢你的想法，就是我们基于过去所有已有的成果继续前进，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.57,0:22:27.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so if I think about full self-driving as an example, we talked about it for a decade, and we really didn't get there, right?\N就拿完全自动驾驶作为例子，我们讨论了十年，但真正实现却一直没做到，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.24,0:22:33.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,But all of the sudden, like you go on Twitter, everybody experiencing Tesla FSD, experiencing Waymo, we're here.\N但突然之间，你上推特一看，人人都在体验特斯拉 FSD，体验 Waymo，我们已经到了这一步。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.99,0:22:36.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Somebody asked me how was the drive here this morning?\N有人问我今天早上开车过来感觉怎么样？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.16,0:22:42.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I said, I don't know cuz I got in my car and I hit FSD and I didn't pay any attention until we pulled into the parking garage, right?\N我说，我不知道，因为我上车后就开启了 FSD，一路都没怎么注意，直到我们驶入停车场，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.20,0:22:44.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was working the whole way here.\N我一路上都在工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.36,0:22:51.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but if I think about that in the fields of science, the breakthroughs that are going to come in the fields of pharma and genetics, right?\N嗯，但如果我从科学领域来看，医药和基因领域的突破，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.34,0:22:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've been laying down the tracks for 30 years.\N我们已经为此铺了三十年的路。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.68,0:22:57.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to break through on on on a lot of massive cures for the world.\N我们将突破许多重大疾病的治疗，为世界带来深远影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.64,0:23:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course, ChatGPT is already helping parents plan their day and solve their kids health issue and helping them uh get get better educated.\N当然，ChatGPT 已经在帮助父母规划一天的行程，解决孩子的健康问题，并帮助他们获得更好的教育。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.44,0:23:12.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um talk to us a little bit though as to why that's having such a hard time breaking through, Jensen.\N但黄仁勋，能不能跟我们聊一聊，为什么这方面的进展会如此艰难？
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.46,0:23:17.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have all of these things that are out there improving lives and that are right around the corner.\N我们已经拥有许多正在改善生活、就在眼前的创新技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.47,0:23:23.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that that's kind of curious to me as to why that's not breaking through.\N所以这让我感到有些好奇，为什么这些进展还没有真正突破。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.32,0:23:27.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I guess I guess um let me take a shot at it.\N我猜，让我试着回答一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.05,0:23:31.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and you know, we'll we'll ultimately not really know.\N毕竟，我们最终可能也未必真正清楚。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.76,0:23:35.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I I've spoken to a lot of people.\N我和很多人谈过。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.28,0:23:36.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,They told me what they thought.\N他们告诉我他们的想法。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.32,0:23:42.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, one of the one of the things of course is is a AI or superintelligence.\N比如，当然，人工智能或超级智能就是其中之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.21,0:23:44.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is a is soft matter.\N它是一种软性存在。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.32,0:23:44.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.84,0:23:47.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't look you can't see it.\N你看不到它，也摸不到它。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.20,0:23:51.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so you got the whole world talking about this technology, but you can't see it.\N而且全世界都在讨论这项技术，但你却看不到它。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.77,0:23:52.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't touch it.\N你无法触摸它。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.64,0:23:52.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.00,0:23:55.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And even though they're already benefiting from it.\N尽管他们已经从中获益。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.08,0:23:57.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,When they do search, they're already benefiting from it.\N搜索时，他们已经在受益。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.06,0:23:58.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,When they go shopping, they're benefiting from it.\N购物时，他们也在受益。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.96,0:24:01.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,When they're when they're using Netflix, they're benefiting from it.\N使用 Netflix 时，他们也在受益。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.76,0:24:04.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, you go to Walmart, you're benefiting from it.\N你知道，去沃尔玛购物时，你也在受益。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.89,0:24:13.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the the fact that FedEx is getting getting stuff to us, you know, It's all leveraging superintelligence and accelerated compute today.\N比如联邦快递能及时把东西送到我们手上，这背后全都在利用今天的超级智能和加速计算。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.49,0:24:15.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we don't do a very good job telling that story.\N但我们并没有很好地讲好这个故事。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.00,0:24:18.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I often think that life is they're benefiting from it.\N我常常觉得，他们其实一直在从中获益。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.19,0:24:19.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just it's invisible.\N只是它太隐形了。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.40,0:24:19.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.76,0:24:25.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if we shut off the data centers and shut off superintelligence for for a weekend, I think everybody would notice.\N如果我们关闭数据中心并暂停超级智能一周，我想每个人都会注意到。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.92,0:24:26.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.28,0:24:26.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N是吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.55,0:24:29.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know you had a question about robotics in particular though.\N我知道你特别想问关于机器人技术的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.16,0:24:29.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.55,0:24:35.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,I guess you you've you've said notably said a few times this year that the chat GPT moment for robotics is here.\N我猜你今年已经多次明确表示，机器人领域的“ChatGPT时刻”已经到来。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.54,0:24:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think you've also you you've also said that it could be your next hundred billion dollar market.\N而且我认为你也说过，这可能成为你下一个百亿美元市场。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:40.32,0:24:47.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I guess what are you seeing now in the inflection point in this year Yeah. that this is around the corner?\N那我想问一下，你现在看到的这个转折点，为什么觉得今年就快到了？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.16,0:24:52.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I I understated the hundred billion dollars because we're we're already the first six months of this year,\N对，我低估了百亿美元，因为今年才过去六个月，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:52.09,0:24:54.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,we did ten billion dollars in physical AI.\N我们在物理 AI 领域已经实现了十亿美元的营收。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.32,0:25:02.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Physical AI is basically you know, AI that's somehow interacting with the physical world and it could be photon photon counting CT machines,\N物理 AI 基本上就是指某种与物理世界产生交互的 AI，比如光子计数 CT 机，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.67,0:25:09.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,it could be ultrasounds, it could be um new imaging radars, next generation of 5G.\N可能是超声波，也可能是新型成像雷达，或是下一代5G。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.20,0:25:09.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.56,0:25:13.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not only does it understand radio waves, it's going to understand signals of all kinds.\N它不仅能理解无线电波，还能理解各种类型的信号。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.12,0:25:16.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a sensing network.\N这是一个感知网络。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.16,0:25:22.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um of course robotics, self-driving cars, manufacturing systems, visual inspections, uh you know,\N比如机器人、自动驾驶汽车、制造系统、视觉检测，还有你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.42,0:25:29.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean geo geo spatial satellites um imaging the world and and reconstructing it into 3D and and so so\N比如地理空间卫星对地球成像，并将其重建为三维模型，等等。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.60,0:25:40.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's there's basically if you look at the entire electromagnetic spectrum there's AI stuff going on from visible to invisible spectrums,\N如果你纵观整个电磁波谱，从可见光到不可见光，AI都在其中发挥作用。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.96,0:25:41.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.96,0:25:46.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so so we and we're doing work across that entire thing.\N所以我们正在整个领域内开展工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.94,0:25:52.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,That and and and and as an AI, there's there's a the perception part of it,\N作为AI，它包含感知部分，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.50,0:25:56.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's the reasoning part of it and then there's the planning and actuation part of it.\N推理部分，以及规划与执行部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:56.56,0:26:02.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you finally get into planning and actuation, then that's self-driving cars and robotics and things like that,\N当你真正进入规划与执行阶段时，就涉及自动驾驶汽车、机器人等应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.14,0:26:08.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, in in warehouse delivery vehicles, pick and place robots that you don't have to program,\N你知道，在仓库配送车辆和无需编程的抓取放置机器人中，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.40,0:26:14.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, as as precisely because it learns by itself, you know, all the way to people talking about consumer robots,\N你知道，正因为它们能自我学习，所以人们开始谈论消费级机器人，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.44,0:26:17.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, coming into your house, you know, making your bed and things.\N你知道，它们会走进你的家，帮你整理床铺等等。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.66,0:26:23.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so or health care robots, hospital robots, lots of really good examples there.\N还有医疗机器人、医院机器人，那里有很多非常出色的例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.36,0:26:34.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Precisely delivering exactly your prescription to the patient um having having robotic care literally 24/7 every single\N精准地将你的处方送到患者手中，让机器人全天候24/7地提供护理，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.97,0:26:41.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,second um to to keep patients safe um and so just lots and lots of great examples,\N时刻保障患者安全，所以这样的优秀案例还有很多。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:41.55,0:26:44.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,entire surgical rooms that are going to be completely robotic.\N整个手术室都将实现完全自动化。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.56,0:26:44.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.00,0:26:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so lots of great technology being deployed.\N因此，大量优秀技术正在被部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.00,0:26:53.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so if you look at this whole thing, we're the world's largest physical AI company.\N所以如果你看整个局面，我们是全球最大的物理AI公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.33,0:26:55.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,We We did $10 billion in the first 6 months.\N我们在前六个月就实现了100亿美元的营收。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:56.02,0:26:59.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did $10 billion in the last year.\N我们在去年一年也实现了100亿美元的营收。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.20,0:27:00.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that was our first $10 billion year.\N那也是我们首个100亿美元的年份。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.00,0:27:02.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,The year before that we did five.\N那之前一年，我们做了五次。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.00,0:27:03.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好，明白了？
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.34,0:27:06.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we went five, 10, let's say we did 20.\N于是我们试了五次、十次，假设我们试了二十次。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.00,0:27:07.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Who knows?\N谁知道呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.63,0:27:10.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So maybe the 100 was a little understated.\N所以，也许100这个数字稍微有点保守了。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.04,0:27:18.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and I I think the reasoning part of it is is everything that matters to us in the final analysis touches the physical world.\N而且我认为，其中的推理部分，最终所有对我们来说重要的事情，都与物理世界息息相关。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.67,0:27:20.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and we live in the physical world.\N而且我们生活在这个物理世界中。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.74,0:27:27.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I I think the the market opportunity for bringing uh software, computing,\N因此我认为，将软件和计算带入市场的机遇非常巨大。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.02,0:27:35.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,intelligence into an industry that largely historically was mechanical, electrical, that's a big opportunity.\N将智能引入长期以来以机械、电气为主的产业，这是一个巨大的机遇。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.69,0:27:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, look at look at obviously what Elon has done to the to the automotive industry.\N我的意思是，看看埃隆对汽车工业所做的事情，显而易见。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.88,0:27:44.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Turned it into essentially a computing industry, a technology industry.\N将其转变为一个本质上是计算产业、技术产业的行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.65,0:27:48.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I think every car company's going to be a technology company.\N所以我认为每家汽车公司都将成为一家科技公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.68,0:27:52.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every shipping and receiving's company the logistics company's going to be a technology company.\N每家物流和收发公司也都会成为一家科技公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.13,0:27:53.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm super excited for FedEx.\N我对联邦快递充满期待。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.39,0:27:54.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're obviously going to be an AI company.\N他们显然会成为一家AI公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.04,0:27:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're obviously going to be a technology company.\N他们显然会成为一家科技公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.40,0:28:01.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Walmart obviously going to be a technology company an AI company.\N沃尔玛显然会成为一家科技公司和AI公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.20,0:28:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So super excited for them.\N所以我为他们感到非常兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.84,0:28:08.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,The entire telecommunications industry will be reinvented again into an into a technology industry.\N整个电信行业将再次被彻底重塑，转变为一家科技行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.72,0:28:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,They were a technology industry a long time ago.\N他们很久以前就是一家科技行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.28,0:28:12.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,They became a services industry.\N他们后来变成了服务行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:12.50,0:28:14.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're going to be a technology industry again.\N他们将再次成为一家科技行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.60,0:28:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm delighted to work with AT&T and Verizon and all, you know, the and in Europe around the world as they reinvent themselves.\N我很高兴能与AT&T、威瑞森以及全球各地的公司，包括欧洲的，一起合作，见证他们重塑自身。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.12,0:28:26.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so you you take a look at every one of these industries that touch the physical world.\N嗯，所以你看看这些触及物理世界的各个行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.34,0:28:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I there's a a great idea for reinventing them with AI.\N而且我有个很棒的想法，可以用人工智能重新定义它们。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.20,0:28:35.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we we um I was just in Washington weird, you know, people put us in chips.\N你知道，我刚从华盛顿回来，挺奇怪的，人们总把我们和芯片联系在一起。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.40,0:28:36.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.20,0:28:40.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, and and so we're actually in warehousing logistics.\N事实上，我们正在涉足仓储物流领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.48,0:28:41.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.32,0:28:42.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're in healthcare.\N我们在医疗健康领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.64,0:28:43.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.04,0:28:44.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're in automotive.\N我们在汽车领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.28,0:28:46.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're in telecommunications.\N我们在电信领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.12,0:28:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.72,0:28:48.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every industry in the Yeah.\N每一个行业，嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.06,0:28:52.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so so we're in light we're we're in we're in life sciences, you know,\N而且我们正处于生命科学领域，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.08,0:28:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,and so so all these entertainment obviously for a long for a long time Nvidia was really vastly an entertainment company,\N所以长期以来，这些娱乐业务显然都是英伟达的核心业务，英伟达本质上是一家娱乐公司，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.16,0:29:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, and so so each one of these verticals uh Nvidia has has a massive stack that's inside of it and and we're very deep in the ecosystem.\N你知道，这些垂直领域中，英伟达都拥有庞大的技术栈，我们深度嵌入在生态系统中。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.00,0:29:12.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and we have excellent partnerships there.\N而且我们在那里拥有出色的合作伙伴关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.47,0:29:18.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you know, one of these days, you know, people might not categorize us as a chip company anymore.\N所以有一天，人们可能不再把我们归类为芯片公司了。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.20,0:29:25.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,would be to take the Alpha IO automotive I guess playbook and insert it into each one of these industries.\N就是把 Alpha IO 汽车行业的成功模式，应用到每一个行业当中。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:25.16,0:29:29.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's that's the final that's the final um contribution.\N对，这就是最终的贡献。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.26,0:29:37.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,But in each one of these it takes three computers to build a physical AI platform and so so you need you need a computer to create the brain,\N但在每个领域，构建一个物理 AI 平台都需要三台计算机，因此你需要一台计算机来打造大脑，
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.64,0:29:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's the training system.\N那就是训练系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.52,0:29:44.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,But very importantly and this is where where you're going to see the labs also do this.\N但至关重要的是，这也是你将看到实验室也这样做的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.80,0:29:49.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um they need to build a digital twin of the internet.\N他们需要构建一个互联网的数字孪生体。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.52,0:29:54.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that they don't have to put their AI agents out into the internet to learn how to use it.\N这样他们就不必把 AI 智能体放到互联网上，去学习如何使用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.60,0:29:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so just like we we created Omniverse as the digital twin of warehouses and\N因此，我们就像创建仓库的数字孪生体一样，打造了Omniverse。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.24,0:30:03.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,buildings and cities in the physical world we put our robot into the digital twin,\N我们将物理世界中的建筑和城市导入数字孪生，让我们的机器人在其中运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.92,0:30:05.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,the digital twin learns how to be a robot,\N数字孪生学会了如何成为一台机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.78,0:30:09.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then we deploy it into the last computer, which is the computer that's inside,\N然后我们将它部署到最后一台计算机上，也就是内部的那台计算机。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.67,0:30:13.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, for example, a robot or a car or surgical instrument or whatever it is.\N你知道，比如机器人、汽车、手术器械，或者其他任何东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.96,0:30:20.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it takes three robots, three computers and three complete stacks and we build complete stacks for each one of them.\N因此我们需要三台机器人、三台计算机和三套完整的系统，为每台机器人搭建一套完整的系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.27,0:30:22.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're the only company in the world that does that.\N我们是全球唯一一家做到这一点的公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.19,0:30:30.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then if you're a company that that wants to build it end to end, you could use two or three or you know, one of our computers, we don't care.\N如果你是一家希望从头到尾自己搭建的公司，可以使用两台、三台，或者我们其中一台计算机，我们都不介意。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.33,0:30:32.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so and so each one of our computer has its own software stack.\N因此，我们每台计算机都有自己的软件栈。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.99,0:30:35.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We do the same across all of our verticals.\N我们在所有业务领域都采用同样的做法。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.12,0:30:43.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but of course these capabilities cut both ways, which is why um you know, we hear a lot of people talking about safety.\N但当然，这些能力具有两面性，这也是为什么我们经常听到很多人在谈论安全问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.67,0:30:47.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've been highly critical of the doomer narrative.\N你一直对悲观论调持强烈批评态度。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.36,0:30:50.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can only get there if you build the technology responsibly.\N只有负责任地构建技术，你才能到达那里。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.08,0:30:50.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.88,0:30:54.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the first thing is build the technology responsibly.\N所以，第一件事就是负责任地构建技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.72,0:30:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.68,0:30:56.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Notice the word build.\N注意“构建”这个词。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:56.69,0:30:58.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's an engineering word.\N这是一个工程术语。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.08,0:30:58.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.88,0:31:01.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's about technology, it's about engineering.\N这关乎技术，也关乎工程。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.12,0:31:07.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Engineers, scientists, researchers, we have to build this technology safely, responsibly.\N工程师、科学家、研究人员，我们必须安全、负责任地构建这项技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.01,0:31:10.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and the question is, can you?\N问题是，你能做到吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.24,0:31:13.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the the the answer is absolutely yes.\N答案是，绝对可以。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.40,0:31:16.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because if you can't, then you shouldn't build it at all.\N因为如果你做不到，那就根本不该去构建它。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.80,0:31:17.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course.\N当然。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.80,0:31:21.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we either have to believe we can or we shouldn't build it.\N所以，我们要么相信自己能做到，要么就不该去建造它。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.75,0:31:22.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.08,0:31:23.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I believe we can.\N因此，我相信我们能做到。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.20,0:31:26.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, here, let me just reason about it with you.\N所以，让我来和你一起分析一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.08,0:31:36.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the first part of it is they say some people say that that AI is is uncontrollable because it's impossible to align perfectly.\N首先，有人说人工智能无法控制，因为完美对齐是不可能的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.58,0:31:39.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alignment means this for all the audience.\N对齐的意思，对所有观众来说就是这个。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.24,0:31:42.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, you tell somebody, um, I want you to do this.\N你告诉某人，呃，我想让你做这件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.36,0:31:42.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.84,0:31:44.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the mission is clear.\N所以，目标非常明确。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:45.04,0:31:45.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:45.28,0:31:46.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,The mission is clear.\N目标非常明确。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.56,0:31:49.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, um, I it's clear to you.\N而且，呃，这对你来说很清楚。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.52,0:31:49.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.84,0:31:52.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because you said it in English, okay?\N因为你用英语说出来了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:52.20,0:31:55.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, it could be, uh, I want you to solve this quadratic equation.\N所以，可能是，呃，我想让你解这个二次方程。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.48,0:31:55.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.00,0:31:58.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the the mission is to solve the quadratic equation.\N所以，任务就是解这个二次方程。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.43,0:32:00.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,The the alignment is how do you do it?\N对齐的问题是，你该怎么解？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.42,0:32:01.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are many ways to do it.\N有很多方法可以解。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.93,0:32:03.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,For example, you memorized it.\N比如说，你背下来了。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.76,0:32:04.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.32,0:32:04.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.66,0:32:07.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the answer is, you know, whatever it is.\N所以，答案就是，你知道的，不管是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.96,0:32:12.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, or uh, you saw the answer in a textbook, so you looked it up.\N嗯，或者你是在教科书里看到了答案，所以去查了一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.44,0:32:12.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.96,0:32:13.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.41,0:32:15.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, you refer to a reference.\N嗯，你参考了参考资料。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.68,0:32:16.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.08,0:32:19.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or you went to a drawer and you you you know that drawer had all the answers.\N或者你去了一个抽屉，你知道那个抽屉里有所有答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:20.04,0:32:21.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,You open the drawer, you picked out the answer, okay?\N你打开抽屉，拿出答案，明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.82,0:32:23.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some people call that cheating.\N有些人管这叫作弊。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.27,0:32:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, I call that opening the drawer and retrieving the answer.\N嗯，我管这叫打开抽屉，取出答案。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.28,0:32:26.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.60,0:32:26.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.89,0:32:28.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's what computers do.\N这正是计算机所做的。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.32,0:32:31.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a lot of different ways you could solve that problem, okay?\N解决那个问题有很多不同的方法，明白吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.14,0:32:33.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, of course, that one is very explicit.\N当然，那个非常明确。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:33.60,0:32:34.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here's another one.\N再来一个。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.48,0:32:36.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, be successful in life.\N啊，人生要成功。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.72,0:32:37.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,The mission is easy to say.\N使命很容易说。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.90,0:32:40.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in fact we say it to each other all the time.\N事实上，我们经常彼此这么说。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.16,0:32:46.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we say it to our children, we say it to our our friends, let's do our best to to contribute to society.\N我们常对孩子、对朋友说，要尽自己最大努力为社会做贡献。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.54,0:32:49.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, now the question is how.\N现在的问题是，该怎么做。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.88,0:32:51.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are so many ways.\N方式多得数不胜数。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.50,0:32:59.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you reasonably align and everybody's culture and background and some people think that contributing to society means to be generous,\N如何合理地协调每个人的文化背景和价值观？有些人认为，回馈社会就意味着慷慨大方。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:59.94,0:33:00.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,to be kind.\N友善一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.77,0:33:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some people might mean that contribute to society make a lot of money and and then give philanthropic.\N有些人可能认为，为社会做贡献的人会赚很多钱，然后进行慈善捐赠。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.76,0:33:09.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some people might so and so forth.\N有些人可能会这样想，等等。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.23,0:33:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Isn't that right?\N没错吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.00,0:33:10.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.32,0:33:10.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.58,0:33:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And some people might just think that that building a company alone is is or doing something alone is is a sufficient contribution to society.\N有些人可能只是认为，独自创办一家公司，或独自做某件事，就已经是对社会的足够贡献了。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.68,0:33:21.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Creating a beautiful piece of art or all of it is true.\N创造一件美丽的艺术品，这确实是真的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.88,0:33:22.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Correct.\N正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:22.32,0:33:24.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the question is what's the alignment?\N所以问题在于，什么是契合？
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.62,0:33:29.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it just depends on your background, your culture, maybe has something to do with where you live, where you came from.\N这完全取决于你的背景、文化，也许还和你生活的地方、成长的地方有关。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.95,0:33:31.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's just infinite number of ways.\N有无穷无尽的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.00,0:33:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so my point is this.\N所以我的观点是：
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.16,0:33:37.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alignment is going to be a forever problem.\N契合将是一个永恒的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.32,0:33:38.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.20,0:33:44.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,If we depend on perfect alignment in order to ensure safety, then we're never going to get there.\N如果我们依赖完全对齐来确保安全，那么我们就永远无法实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.24,0:33:46.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the answer is this.\N所以答案是这样的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:46.28,0:33:54.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,The way we treat the way we think about babies and when we we're raising kids and you know, we have pets or whatever it is, employees.\N我们对待婴儿、教育孩子，以及养宠物或管理员工的方式，都体现了这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.60,0:33:55.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.32,0:33:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,You start with containment.\N你从隔离开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.32,0:34:02.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,You give them the rights that the access to tools, the access to information,\N给他们使用工具、获取信息的权限，
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.82,0:34:07.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,the access to whatever responsibility capabilities that they have, funds, resources.\N以及他们所承担职责所需的资源和资金。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:07.16,0:34:11.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,You give them access based on the job that you ask them to do.\N你根据他们被要求完成的工作来授予访问权限。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.16,0:34:13.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,You start out with zero trust.\N从零信任开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.29,0:34:15.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you hire somebody, you start out with zero trust.\N雇用一个人时，你从零信任开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.35,0:34:20.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you have a baby that's 1 year old, you put them in a playpen, you assume zero trust.\N当你有一个一岁的婴儿时，你会把他放进婴儿围栏，假设零信任。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.20,0:34:26.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you zero trust, you give them minimum rights and you expand that boundary as you learn more.\N因此你要实施零信任，只给予最小权限，并随着了解的深入逐步扩大边界。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.89,0:34:31.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so when whenever we have a new AI, we have to assume the same thing.\N所以每当出现新的AI时，我们都必须假设同样的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.15,0:34:41.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Whenever you're testing an AI, zero trust, minimum boundaries, minimum rights, and you expand it as you test and give yourself confidence.\N无论何时测试AI，都要坚持零信任原则，设置最小边界和最小权限，并在测试过程中逐步扩展，以建立信心。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.15,0:34:46.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, containment, very tight containment is really important to any autonomous system.\N因此，隔离至关重要，对任何自主系统来说，必须实现高度严格的隔离。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:46.28,0:34:49.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Second thing you do, uh monitoring.\N第二件事，是监控。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.88,0:34:51.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the monitoring has to be out of band.\N而监控必须是带外的。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.41,0:34:56.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because if you're if you tell an intelligent person, "Hey, listen,\N原因在于，如果你对一个聪明的人说：“嘿，听着，
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.26,0:34:59.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to sit here and watch you do your work to make sure you're doing it right."\N我就坐在这里观察你工作，确保你做对了。”
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.12,0:34:59.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.76,0:35:00.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.72,0:35:06.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm going to sit here and watch you make sure that you're serving customers properly and that you're working hard enough.\N我就坐在这里观察你，确保你正确服务客户，并且足够努力工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.71,0:35:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.52,0:35:12.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,That that autonomous system is going to behave differently than when you're not watching.\N那个自主系统在你不在场时的行为会有所不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:12.28,0:35:14.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like Brad's in the room with me or not.\N就像布拉德在我身边或不在身边一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.04,0:35:15.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.80,0:35:16.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.56,0:35:17.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.06,0:35:21.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so the the the monitoring has to be out of band and it has to have the\N所以监控必须是带外的，而且必须能够
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.58,0:35:29.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,ability to observe that the autonomous system is doing something that was inconsistent with the policy or inconsistent with alignment,\N观察到自主系统的行为是否与策略或对齐要求不一致，
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.23,0:35:32.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you have the ability to either escalate or shut it down.\N并且你有能力进行升级或直接关停。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.92,0:35:33.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.24,0:35:34.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just turn off.\N直接关掉就行。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.13,0:35:37.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so those kind of capabilities have to exist.\N所以这类能力必须存在。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.74,0:35:39.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's engineering.\N这就是工程。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.13,0:35:40.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's technology.\N这就是技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:40.37,0:35:41.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's possible.\N而且这是可能的。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.32,0:35:43.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we we announced it recently called Open Shell.\N我们最近宣布了它，名为 Open Shell。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.39,0:35:45.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have, you know, over 100 100 companies now joining us.\N目前已有超过100家公司加入我们。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:46.02,0:35:49.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've got lots and lots of activity around the world because everybody wants the same thing.\N全球各地都涌现出大量活动，因为每个人都想要同样的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.40,0:35:56.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Starting at the highest level, you know, when I looked around the table at the White House, Yeah. um everybody around that table, right?\N从最高层面来看，当我环顾白宫的会议桌时，是的，桌边的每个人，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:57.04,0:35:57.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're parents.\N他们都是父母。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:57.94,0:35:58.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have kids.\N他们都有孩子。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.78,0:36:06.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think there's this view in the country that there are some leaders of super intelligence that are just yoloing, that don't really care.\N我觉得国内有一种看法，认为一些超级智能的领导者只是在盲目冒险，根本不在乎。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.56,0:36:07.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're being reckless.\N他们正在鲁莽行事。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.54,0:36:09.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,They just want to grab all the money.\N他们只想攫取所有金钱。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.17,0:36:16.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And yet when I looked around their table that table, there wasn't a person in there that I saw that wants to be reckless, that wants to yolo.\N但当我环顾那张桌子时，我发现里面没有一个人是想鲁莽行事、想盲目冒险的。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.85,0:36:22.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,In fact, everybody there wanted to find the right balance between fast and safe.\N事实上，那里的每个人都想在快速和安全之间找到正确的平衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.04,0:36:24.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,That was the president's directive.\N这是总统的指示。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.55,0:36:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I we we debated a little bit what that meant.\N我们曾就这句指示的具体含义进行过一些讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.16,0:36:28.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.61,0:36:32.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are different versions of how to implement that.\N实现这一点的方式有多种。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.19,0:36:38.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, you know, what would you say to the American public who fears that we have a reckless president or reckless leaders?\N但你知道，面对那些担心我们有鲁莽总统或鲁莽领导人的美国公众，你会怎么回应？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.92,0:36:40.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did you see any evidence of that?\N你看到过这方面的证据吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.35,0:36:41.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have kids.\N你有孩子。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:41.18,0:36:46.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you worry about the future that you're bringing into existence with superintelligence?\N你是否担心，超级智能正在塑造的未来会带来隐患？
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.84,0:36:51.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Safety and security technology Right. are part of AI.\N安全与保障技术确实是人工智能的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.96,0:36:52.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.00,0:37:01.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's some weird formulation that AI technology and safety and security are orthogonal.\N有一种奇怪的说法，认为人工智能技术与安全和保障是相互独立的。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:01.48,0:37:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:02.00,0:37:06.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's kind of like the airbags and the and the braking system Right.\N就像安全气囊和制动系统一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.68,0:37:11.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,and the radars, the cameras, um the ABS, uh the the the lane keeping.\N还有雷达、摄像头、ABS、车道保持功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.86,0:37:15.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of that technology is somehow independent of the car.\N所有这些技术在某种程度上都独立于汽车本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:15.20,0:37:16.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right. understand what I'm saying?\N对，明白我的意思了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.36,0:37:16.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.60,0:37:18.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,The only thing that matters to the car is the engine.\N对汽车来说，唯一重要的是发动机。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.96,0:37:19.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:19.84,0:37:23.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,In fact, the whole car is part of the car's technology.\N实际上，整辆车都是汽车技术的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.74,0:37:24.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,When I say Right.\N当我说“对”的时候。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:25.00,0:37:30.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,to accelerate AI's technology, what I mean by that is we need to accelerate the security technology.\N为了加速AI技术的发展，我的意思是，我们需要加速安全技术的发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:30.98,0:37:33.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have to accelerate the safety technology.\N我们必须加速安全技术的发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.21,0:37:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,They all have to be accelerated.\N所有这些都必须加速。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.36,0:37:35.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.72,0:37:39.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you ask me right now, I think everybody would say, "Let's accelerate security.\N如果现在问我，我认为每个人都会说：“让我们加速安全。”
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.40,0:37:41.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's accelerate safety technology."\N让我们加速安全技术。”
Dialogue: 0,0:37:41.38,0:37:43.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nobody says, "No, let's pace that."\N没人会说：“不，我们放慢点。”
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.60,0:37:44.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:44.12,0:37:45.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,We should accelerate that.\N我们应该加速这个。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.57,0:37:47.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's all part of the same thing.\N这都是同一件事的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:47.78,0:37:52.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't separate capability, functionality from safety and security.\N你无法将能力、功能与安全和防护分开。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.45,0:37:53.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,They go as one.\N它们是一体的。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:53.24,0:37:53.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:53.92,0:37:58.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when you deliver the service, nobody's going to say, "You know, good good uh you know,\N当你提供服务时，没人会说：“你知道，不错不错，你知道，”
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.50,0:38:03.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I really like the the uh the functionality of your service, but boy, is it you know, wrecking havoc."\N我真的很喜欢你们服务的功能，但天哪，它简直太破坏性了。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.00,0:38:04.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.28,0:38:06.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so I I think it's all one thing.\N所以我认为这其实是一回事。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:06.68,0:38:07.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.08,0:38:11.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we treat it as all one thing, and and the industry has to treat it as one thing.\N我们把它当作一回事来对待，整个行业也必须这样看待。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.41,0:38:16.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when we say accelerate, we have to mean accelerating the entire package.\N当我们说加速时，必须是指加速整个体系。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.03,0:38:18.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And right now Including the safety.\N而现在，包括安全在内。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.44,0:38:20.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Including Right. especially the safety.\N包括安全，尤其是安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.52,0:38:21.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,You mentioned pacing.\N你提到了节奏控制。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.76,0:38:22.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Especially safety.\N尤其是安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.96,0:38:23.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know this.\N你知道的。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.71,0:38:27.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some people read Pacing the Frontier by Dario um and thought that meant slowing down.\N有些人读了达里奥的《掌控前沿》后，以为这意味着要放慢速度。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.04,0:38:32.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I thought a funny moment in the room was when the president called on his new best friend Dario.\N我觉得房间里一个有趣的小插曲是，总统提到了他的新朋友达里奥。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:32.70,0:38:34.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,He He referred to him in that way.\N他就是那样称呼他的。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:34.56,0:38:39.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he said, you know, explain to me, you know, the your version of fast and safe.\N然后他说，你知道的，给我解释一下，你对快速且安全的理解。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.24,0:38:45.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Dario started off by saying, "Mr. President, you said whoever wins AI wins."\N达里奥一开始就说：“总统先生，你说过，谁赢了AI，谁就赢了未来。”
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.00,0:38:46.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N是吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.48,0:38:54.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he said that we're all speeding up, that they're speeding up, that they want to go fast, that they want to, you know, win the race with China.\N他说我们都在加速，他们也在加速，他们想快点前进，想赶在与中国竞争中取胜。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:54.95,0:38:59.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,But also acknowledge that along the way we just, to your point you just made,\N但同时，也必须承认，正如你刚才提到的，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.11,0:39:03.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have to make sure the safety systems are also speeding up and also keeping pace.\N我们必须确保安全系统也在同步加速，保持同步。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:03.20,0:39:06.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I thought that was an important moment where you had, you know,\N所以我觉得这是一个重要时刻，你明白吗，
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.66,0:39:11.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,because I think people have positioned him as though he's in opposition, right, to this.\N因为我觉得人们一直把他当成与此对立的角色，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.13,0:39:14.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,But it seemed to me that you were all very much on the same page.\N但在我看来，你们其实非常一致。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:14.97,0:39:22.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,You I You went to the cabinet room with him and and Greg and the other Frontier Labs to sign, uh you know, this agreement.\N你和他、格雷格，以及另外几家前沿实验室的人一起去了内阁会议室，签署那个协议。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:22.42,0:39:26.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Was there any chatter, you know, in that room about differences of opinion?\N那个房间里有没有人讨论过意见分歧？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:26.58,0:39:29.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or was everybody, uh you obviously got it signed.\N还是说大家都很顺利地签了字？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:29.42,0:39:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did anybody have to be put in a headlock?\N有没有人需要被按住头？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.20,0:39:32.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or did everybody go willingly?\N还是大家都心甘情愿地参与了？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.92,0:39:37.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, everybody was very very constructive, very productive.\N没有，大家都非常建设性，非常高效。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.99,0:39:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um I I I think that that without exception, everybody um is dedicated to advancing the industry safely and securely.\N我想，毫不例外，所有人都致力于安全、稳妥地推进这个行业发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.32,0:39:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because if it's not safe, it's not secure, the functionality will never get a chance to speak.\N原因在于，如果不安全、不稳健，功能就永远没有机会展现。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.68,0:39:56.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the capability will never get a get a chance to shine.\N因此，能力也永远无法得到彰显。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:56.74,0:40:02.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we have to We know that the priorities are at all times safety and security.\N所以我们必须始终把安全与安保放在首位。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.19,0:40:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course, recognizing that this industry came through a transition just recently.\N当然，我们也意识到这个行业刚刚经历了一次转型。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.52,0:40:07.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.88,0:40:09.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It wasn't but 6 months ago.\N距离那件事才过去六个月而已。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:09.32,0:40:10.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:10.32,0:40:11.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,This technology barely worked.\N这项技术几乎无法工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:11.72,0:40:12.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.24,0:40:16.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the functionality and Without functionality capability, what's the point of making it safe and secure?\N所以，如果功能性和无功能性能力都不存在，那让它安全和可靠又有什么意义呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.56,0:40:18.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nobody even cares about it.\N根本没人关心它。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:18.20,0:40:23.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the obviously the first the first job of AI is to to demonstrate it could do something useful.\N因此，AI 的首要任务显然是证明它能做点有用的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.31,0:40:23.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.63,0:40:26.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it really reached that point 6 months ago.\N而实际上，它在六个月前就已经达到了那个阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:26.09,0:40:31.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so now it really wants to be deployed and and that and broadly deployed.\N现在它真的渴望被部署，并且广泛部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.50,0:40:38.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so there's no question that the industry the entire industry now has a has a strategic imperative,\N因此，整个行业现在都面临一个战略性的紧迫需求，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.06,0:40:44.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,an incredible imperative, and great urgency to make sure that whatever we deploy is safe and secure.\N一个极其紧迫的需求，以及巨大的紧迫感，确保我们所部署的一切都是安全和可靠的。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:44.48,0:40:49.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I think I think everybody has completely convinced capable aligned functionality,\N所以我认为，每个人都已完全意识到，必须具备可靠且对齐的功能性。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:49.99,0:40:54.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,capability, safety, security, they're all at exactly the same place.\N能力、安全、保障，它们都处于完全相同的位置。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:54.50,0:40:55.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Priority number one.\N首要优先事项。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:55.79,0:41:00.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so um I the question is winning.\N所以，呃，我的问题是关于胜利的。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.92,0:41:01.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:01.24,0:41:10.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I would reframe winning not of the technology industry winning, not of just the AI industry winning.\N呃，我会重新定义“胜利”——不是科技行业获胜，也不是人工智能行业获胜。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:10.06,0:41:13.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um America winning means every industry in America winning.\N美国获胜意味着美国所有行业都获胜。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.60,0:41:14.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Healthcare.\N医疗健康。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:14.36,0:41:14.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:14.85,0:41:16.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nothing would give me more joy.\N没有什么能让我更开心了。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:16.11,0:41:21.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,The definition of America winning is when we talk about Lilly winning, Walmart winning,\N美国获胜的定义，就是我们谈论到礼来公司获胜、沃尔玛获胜、
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.64,0:41:26.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,FedEx winning, every single one Boeing winning, um the US military winning.\N联邦快递获胜、波音公司每一家都获胜，美国军方获胜。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.84,0:41:27.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every citizen winning.\N每一位公民都获胜。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:27.72,0:41:29.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every citizen winning.\N每个公民都在赢。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:29.61,0:41:33.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so uh uh our universities winning, our high schools winning.\N于是，我们的大学在赢，我们的高中也在赢。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.09,0:41:35.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know, that's the definition of winning.\N你知道，这就是赢的定义。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:35.76,0:41:41.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,The winning with there is no winning if it's just the technology winning, but nobody used it.\N如果只是技术在赢，但没人使用，那就不算赢。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:41.32,0:41:41.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:41.94,0:41:42.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.56,0:41:49.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,What what The greatest risk is Of course we're going to you know, I I'll just take it I'll just say baseline.\N什么？最大的风险是，当然，我们会知道，我就直接说，基准线。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:49.80,0:41:55.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh there will be no technology there will be no AI technology industry if we don't build it safely and securely.\N如果我们不安全、可靠地建设，就不会有技术，也不会有AI技术产业。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.72,0:41:56.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.06,0:41:58.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,The This is an existential issue for us.\N这对我们来说是一个关乎生存的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:58.80,0:41:59.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.32,0:42:02.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and it'll if we make it an existential industry for everybody else,\N如果我们让这件事对别人都变成关乎生存的产业，
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.72,0:42:05.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,well that's not going to happen because it'll be an existential issue for us first.\N那不可能发生，因为这会首先对我们构成生存威胁。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:05.76,0:42:06.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:06.12,0:42:14.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so having said that, the definition of winning for us and and I you know, this is the this is the part I always have to change a little bit.\N所以，既然这么说，我们对“胜利”的定义是……你知道，这部分我总是得稍微调整一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.40,0:42:14.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.88,0:42:16.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want us to pivot.\N我希望我们能转型。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:16.32,0:42:16.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like that.\N我喜欢这个说法。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.00,0:42:18.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want us to pivot.\N我希望我们能转型。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:18.50,0:42:24.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And when I see AI winning, America AI winning, I'm looking down from, you know,\N当我看到人工智能取得胜利，看到美国的人工智能取得胜利时，我正俯视着……
Dialogue: 0,0:42:24.61,0:42:27.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,these days we spend a lot of time in the air, and we're just looking down.\N现在我们花很多时间在空中，只是在俯瞰大地。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:27.95,0:42:31.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every state's winning, every county's winning, every community is winning, every company's winning.\N每个州都在赢，每个县都在赢，每个社区都在赢，每家公司都在赢。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:31.96,0:42:36.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody won because we could afford to spend more on healthcare, we could afford to spend more on education,\N每个人都赢了，因为我们能负担得起更多医疗支出，能负担得起更多教育投入，
Dialogue: 0,0:42:36.76,0:42:42.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,we could afford to spend more on interstate, you know, commerce, highways, etc. All of the infrastructure of the country.\N能负担得起更多跨州贸易、高速公路等基础设施建设。整个国家的基础设施都在受益。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:42.54,0:42:50.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,What I hear you saying is the definition of winning is that when we look back 25, 30, 40 years from now, the economy needs to be 10 times as large.\N我听你所说的是，胜利的定义在于，当我们回望25年、30年甚至40年后，经济规模必须扩大十倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:50.17,0:42:52.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everybody's lives need to be better.\N每个人的生活都必须变得更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:52.19,0:42:58.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And existential and primary to all of that is that it has to be done in a way that's aligned with human interest.\N而所有这一切的根本和核心在于，必须以符合人类利益的方式实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:58.28,0:43:03.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which This is the last question I have on on on this and I know we have a lot to get to.\N这是我关于这个话题的最后一个提问了，我知道我们还有很多内容要讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:03.68,0:43:07.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Most people don't understand what our security framework it it is in the country.\N大多数人并不理解我们国家的安全框架究竟是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:07.89,0:43:12.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I've said we have the most robust superintelligent framework in the world.\N我曾说过，我们拥有全球最强大的超级智能框架。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.84,0:43:19.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we're we're clearly the only country on the planet that's actually sanctioned a model and pulled it off the shelf with Mythos earlier this year.\N我们是地球上唯一一个真正对模型实施过制裁，并在今年早些时候将其从货架上撤下的国家。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:19.14,0:43:21.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I describe it as a three-legged stool.\N但我会把它描述为一个三足鼎立的框架。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:21.44,0:43:27.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have the frontier model review of every new frontier model by Casey in the Department of Commerce.\N我们有商务部凯西主导的前沿模型审查机制。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.22,0:43:30.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they do all their work if new model's coming out, they review it,\N所以每当有新模型推出时，他们都会进行审查，
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.67,0:43:34.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,they test it for whether or not they think it's going to cause a problem in the marketplace.\N并测试该模型是否可能在市场中引发问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.63,0:43:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now we have the White House Accord on superintelligence that you helped to architect,\N现在我们有你参与设计的白宫超级智能协议，
Dialogue: 0,0:43:39.20,0:43:45.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,internal and external audits, board oversight, and all of the liability that comes with that.\N内部和外部审计、董事会监督，以及随之而来的所有责任。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.86,0:43:52.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then third, we have the SI force now led by Jay Clayton, of course Emil and Scott and Andrew.\N第三，现在由杰伊·克莱顿领导的SI团队，当然还有埃米尔、斯科特和安德鲁。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:52.40,0:43:59.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's doing critical industry coordination, cyber, etc. So these three legs on the stool,\N以及正在开展的关键行业协调工作，包括网络安全等。因此，这个三足鼎立的框架，
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.59,0:44:04.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,um there are people out there I heard Gates recently saying we're not doing, you know, enough.\N我听说盖茨最近提到，我们做得还不够，你知道的。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:04.42,0:44:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need new laws on the books and everything else.\N我们需要出台新的法律，以及其他一切措施。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:07.04,0:44:14.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,That three-legged stool seems like a lot to me in a very short period of time that's come together as a leader of one of the most important companies,\N这个三足鼎立的框架对我来说，在如此短的时间内就形成，作为一家最重要公司之一的领导者，显得非常艰巨。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:14.84,0:44:16.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,obviously, in super intelligence.\N毫无疑问，这在超级智能领域至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.63,0:44:25.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you feel comfortable, right, for that future that we're trying to usher in, that that is a good step forward where we need to be right now?\N你是否觉得，我们正努力推动的未来，这确实是一个正确的前进方向，正是我们现在需要的？
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.24,0:44:31.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, the best way to get to the future is take action quickly.\N是的，通往未来的最佳方式就是迅速采取行动。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:31.55,0:44:32.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:32.15,0:44:41.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and if we if we argue about what is the what's perfect versus what's first.\N如果我们争论什么是完美， versus 什么是第一个。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:41.24,0:44:41.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:41.72,0:44:46.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll end up arguing about perfection and we'll never get there.\N我们最终会陷入对完美的争论，却永远无法达成。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.60,0:44:52.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I love I love the fact that that these three-legged stools are actionable.\N所以我很喜欢这三足鼎立框架的可操作性。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:52.96,0:44:53.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:53.36,0:44:54.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're tangible.\N它们是可感知的。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:54.58,0:44:56.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have real teeth.\N它们有真正的力量。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.08,0:44:56.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.52,0:44:57.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Happening now.\N正在发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:57.48,0:44:58.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's happening right now.\N正在当下发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:58.98,0:45:00.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could We're doing it now.\N你可以说，我们现在就在做。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:00.56,0:45:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're taking action now.\N我们现在正在采取行动。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:02.12,0:45:02.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:02.56,0:45:05.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason we're taking action now is because it's good for our company.\N我们之所以现在采取行动，是因为这对公司有利。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:05.32,0:45:06.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's good for industry.\N对产业有利。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:06.88,0:45:07.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's good for our country.\N对我们的国家有利。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:07.84,0:45:08.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's good for our society.\N对我们的社会有利。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:08.82,0:45:10.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's good all the way around.\N从各方面来看都很好。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:10.10,0:45:16.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if we don't do these things, you know, the outcome the outcome is is less desirable.\N如果我们不这么做，结果显然会更不理想。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.54,0:45:20.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't get to pursue that optimistic future that we all dream dreamt about.\N我们将无法追求那个我们都曾梦想过的乐观未来。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.52,0:45:28.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so if you go back and look at another industry, I don't remember another industry that is it's currently at its current state.\N所以如果你回头看看另一个行业，我想不起还有哪个行业目前处于这种状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:28.44,0:45:29.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:29.12,0:45:33.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And have now formulated all of these cross-company, cross-industrial,\N并且现在已建立起所有这些跨公司、跨行业的，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:33.80,0:45:42.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,government-to-industry coordination to make sure that we we we advance this in a responsible and optimistic way.\N政府与产业之间的协调机制，以确保我们以负责任且乐观的方式推进此事。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.08,0:45:47.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I just think it's so important for people to understand because when I hear senators talking about it on television,\N是的，我认为人们理解这一点非常重要，因为当我听到参议员们在电视上谈论时，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.72,0:45:53.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,on both sides, to be perfectly honest, like they don't to learn about what we're doing here first. don't even know what we're doing.\N无论是哪一方，坦白说，他们都不了解我们在这里正在做什么，甚至根本不知道我们在做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.66,0:45:54.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah.\N是的，没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:54.15,0:45:54.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:45:54.46,0:45:56.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we are doing an extraordinary amount.\N就像我们正在做大量非凡的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:56.54,0:45:58.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And by the way, these are voluntary things.\N顺便说一句，这些事都是自愿的。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.62,0:46:04.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's not going to be a frontier model that gets released that Casey is not reviewing and the Commerce Department\N不会有任何前沿模型被发布，而凯西没有审查，商务部也没有审查的情况出现。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.32,0:46:11.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,is not reviewing and they demonstrated they have the authority under export controls to pull them off the shelf. things.\N他们已经证明，根据出口管制规定，他们有权将这些模型从货架上撤下。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.14,0:46:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,One, come and spend some time in in and and learn what actually has to be done.\N第一，来这儿待一段时间，了解实际需要做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.04,0:46:17.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's the problem?\N问题出在哪里？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.92,0:46:18.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:18.20,0:46:20.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you want a solution, you got to at least understand what the problem is.\N如果你想找到解决方案，至少得先理解问题本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.48,0:46:20.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.80,0:46:21.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:21.15,0:46:22.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so one, come and just learn more.\N所以，来吧，多了解一些。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.00,0:46:23.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got plenty of time.\N我们有充足的时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.76,0:46:29.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,I got all the time in the world for this kind of stuff and and just, you know, come talk to us, come talk to our industry and learn.\N我对这类事情有无限的时间，随时欢迎你来和我们聊聊，和我们的行业交流，来学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.86,0:46:37.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second thing is learn about the solution that we put in place and then and try to see if we can make that if there are ideas to make that better,\N第二点是，了解我们所部署的解决方案，然后看看有没有办法让这个方案变得更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.30,0:46:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,of course, we're all completely open-minded.\N当然，我们完全保持开放心态。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.20,0:46:39.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.48,0:46:41.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, and so but but be constructive.\N你知道，所以，但要提出建设性意见。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.04,0:46:42.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.44,0:46:43.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Be constructive.\N提出建设性意见。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:43.24,0:46:48.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,part of the the the the fourth point on on the accord on super intelligence was this is not static.\N协议中关于超级智能的第四点是，这并非一成不变。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.96,0:46:49.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:49.12,0:46:49.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is dynamic.\N这是动态的。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.04,0:46:50.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.16,0:46:52.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,This group is going to get together routinely.\N这个团队将定期聚在一起。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:52.16,0:46:59.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to update the framework as required when the technology evolves, but I want to move forward now uh to compute.\N当技术演进时，我们会根据需要更新框架，但现在我想先谈谈计算。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:59.09,0:47:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course, long-running agents that work in teams of thousands or millions to solve complicated tasks, it all consumes massively more compute.\N当然，那些长时间运行、成千上万甚至数百万协同工作的智能体，要解决复杂任务，消耗的计算资源极为庞大。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:07.52,0:47:15.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Dylan, our friend as as SemiAnalysis has said we're going to bring on board 43 gigawatts of new AI compute next year.\N丹尼尔，正如 SemiAnalysis 的朋友所说，明年我们将新增 43 吉瓦的 AI 计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:15.94,0:47:19.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just to contextualize it, we'll share a chart with people online.\N为了让大家更好地理解，我们稍后会在线分享一张图表。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.61,0:47:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's more than all of the AI compute that exists in the world today.\N这比目前世界上所有 AI 计算能力的总和还要多。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:24.16,0:47:31.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're going to bring that on board next year, the year after that another 40 gigawatts uh of compute.\N所以，明年我们将部署这部分计算能力，后年再增加 40 吉瓦的计算能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:31.52,0:47:35.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,You are the one you know where every single GPU is allocated.\N你是最清楚的，你知道每一块 GPU 都被分配到了哪里。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.30,0:47:35.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.83,0:47:38.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, as you sit here, does that sound right to you?\N所以，你现在坐在这里，觉得这听起来合理吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:39.04,0:47:42.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you think we're going to bring on that much compute?\N你觉得我们真的能部署这么多计算能力吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:42.49,0:47:44.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and do you think that, you know,\N嗯，那你觉得，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.48,0:47:51.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,some of the things we're hearing out there about permitting permitting issues or bottlenecks in the supply chain or,\N外面听到的那些审批问题、供应链瓶颈，或者
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.29,0:48:00.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, uh local protests uh do Do think the number's going to be materially different than that based upon what you're seeing?\N你知道，当地抗议——你觉得根据你看到的情况，这个数字会有实质性不同吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.44,0:48:04.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I think the demand is definitely there and more.\N我认为需求确实存在，而且还会更多。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.44,0:48:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.92,0:48:06.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The demand is definitely there and more.\N需求确实存在，而且还会更多。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.88,0:48:16.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the challenge, of course, is that there are a lot of obstacles when you when you move from uh when you move from digital to the physical,\N嗯，当然，从数字世界转向物理世界时，会遇到很多障碍，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:16.39,0:48:17.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,there are a lot of obstacles.\N有很多障碍。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:18.04,0:48:18.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:18.40,0:48:20.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,There there land permitting.\N有土地审批的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:20.28,0:48:22.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's power generation that you got to bring online.\N还需要建设发电设施并投入运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:22.81,0:48:28.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um of course, you got to you need construction workers and outfitters and plumbers and you know,\N嗯，当然，还需要建筑工人、安装人员、水管工等等，你知道的。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.80,0:48:31.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,all kinds of Created a million new jobs just building these things.\N各种各样的，仅建造这些设施就创造了百万个新岗位。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:31.68,0:48:37.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Created a million new jobs and and their their skills are their skills are not fungible, you know,\N创造了百万个新岗位，而且他们的技能是不可替代的，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.28,0:48:42.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,they they have a lot of skills and particularly the the ones that are building these $50 billion data centers,\N他们拥有大量技能，尤其是那些正在建设价值500亿美元数据中心的人，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:42.65,0:48:44.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh you're going to want some people with great skills.\N你肯定需要一些技能出众的人。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.96,0:48:45.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.20,0:48:52.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and and there's a critical part of every single one of the build out of these things where where you need some very specific skills.\N而且在建造这些设施的每一个环节中，都有一个关键部分，需要非常特定的技能。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.59,0:48:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so um I I think that and then there's there's of course um uh whatever moratoriums that are that are happening.\N所以我认为，当然，目前存在的任何暂停令。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.16,0:49:06.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um what whatever whatever issues that are that are um uh um that we're seeing around around the country.\N以及全国各地正在出现的各种问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:06.14,0:49:07.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so,\N因此，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:07.12,0:49:12.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think I think this is this is um uh my guess is\N我认为这可能是我的猜测，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:12.10,0:49:19.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,that uh land power shell um uh the the build out resources Mhm.\N土地、电力与厂房的建设资源，嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.44,0:49:23.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh will be one of the the most important obstacles to reaching that.\N将成为实现目标过程中最重要的障碍之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:23.60,0:49:31.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so, so our our company, as you know, now speaking specifically for us, there's several things that we're doing to uh mitigate that.\N而且，正如大家所知，我们公司目前正在采取几项措施来缓解这一问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:31.80,0:49:37.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And one, you know, because we're the only company that serves every CSP, we serve every NCP.\N而且，你知道，因为我们是唯一一家为所有云服务商和所有云提供商提供服务的公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.84,0:49:43.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um uh we have uh uh great enterprise businesses through Dell and HP and Lenovo and others.\N嗯，我们通过戴尔、惠普、联想等公司拥有非常出色的企业业务。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.88,0:49:46.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And because we serve every single industry.\N因为我们服务每一个行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.00,0:49:51.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And we're across the entire uh life cycle of AI.\N而且我们贯穿了AI的整个生命周期。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:52.00,0:49:53.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everything from, you know, of course,\N从你所知的方方面面，当然了，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.32,0:50:02.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,data processing to training to post-training to inference to agentic processing and all of the tool used that we accelerate.\N从数据处理到训练，再到后训练、推理以及代理式处理，所有这些工具我们都在加速。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.76,0:50:08.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, our exposure to our go-to-market is the largest of all.\N你知道，我们在市场推广上的投入是所有公司中最大的。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:08.16,0:50:13.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every every contract manufacturer in the world is working on my behalf.\N全球每一家合同制造商都在为我工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:13.12,0:50:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every go-to-market is is connected to our architecture.\N每个上市策略都与我们的架构紧密相连。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:16.40,0:50:23.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so we have one particular state, one particular community, one particular data center has a hard time.\N因此，有一个特定的州、一个特定的社区、一个特定的数据中心正面临困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:23.44,0:50:26.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, our demand is so much greater than our supply at the moment.\N你知道，目前我们的需求远大于供应。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.80,0:50:30.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll just adjust our supply chain accordingly.\N我们会相应地调整供应链。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:30.08,0:50:38.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other thing that we have and I don't love this answer as much, but as you know, Nvidia is also the infrastructure for the planet.\N另外一点是，我们确实拥有这一点，虽然我不太喜欢这个答案，但正如你所知，英伟达也是全球的基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.31,0:50:48.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so whether it's in Europe or and we we we've got early developments now in Africa, in Central Asia,\N无论是在欧洲，还是我们现在在非洲、中亚，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.44,0:50:53.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,in Southeast Asia, and Latin America, and you know, and the Middle East and so on and so forth.\N东南亚、拉丁美洲，以及中东等地的早期发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:53.47,0:50:58.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I I don't I don't love that that that United States can't keep up.\N所以我不喜欢美国无法跟上的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.02,0:51:02.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,But for our business specifically, we have such a global reach.\N但就我们的业务而言，我们具有如此全球化的覆盖范围。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.80,0:51:06.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and there's build-out demand all around the world.\N全球各地都有建设需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:06.68,0:51:14.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,If we don't build it out here, you know, I think we just all have to recognize that every country in the world would love to have it built out there.\N如果我们不在这里建设，我想我们都必须认识到，世界上每个国家都希望在那里建设。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:14.56,0:51:25.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so and so um I think that that our business specifically is probably the most resilient.\N所以我认为，就我们的业务而言，可能是最具韧性的。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.60,0:51:28.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is is all the things that I mentioned.\N原因就在于我提到的所有这些因素。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:28.26,0:51:31.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we cover the entire spectrum of of AI.\N我们覆盖了人工智能的整个领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:32.00,0:51:34.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We cover the entire spectrum of computing.\N我们覆盖了计算的整个领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:35.04,0:51:41.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're in every single cloud, every single region, you know, and so so the resilience of our company is much greater.\N我们在每一个云服务和每一个区域都有布局，因此我们公司的韧性要强得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:41.12,0:51:44.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I do think that land power shortage is going to be a challenging part next year.\N但我确实认为，明年土地和电力的短缺将会成为一个挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:44.28,0:51:48.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and I guess what I what I what I hear from the street is there's this idea that you know,\N我觉得从街头听到的消息是，大家普遍认为，
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.69,0:51:55.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,maybe there's 50 gigawatts of announced chips that are underway or talked about\N可能有50吉瓦的芯片项目正在推进或被讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:55.55,0:52:01.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,and maybe 35 to 40 gigawatts of land power shell that might come online.\N而可能有35到40吉瓦的土地、电力与厂房资源将上线。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:01.08,0:52:08.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what compute fits into that land power and shell and on what timeline is a question up in the air.\N那么，什么样的计算能力能适配这些土地和电力资源，以及在什么时间表上，目前尚不确定。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:08.84,0:52:09.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:09.12,0:52:20.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I guess like if we think of through the entire and just Clark just just interrupt you there and and I you you know,\N但我想，如果我们从整体来看，克拉克，抱歉打断一下，你明白的，
Dialogue: 0,0:52:20.17,0:52:24.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,of course as you know, Nvidia's architecture is the most productive.\N毫无疑问，英伟达的架构是最高效的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:24.60,0:52:25.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:25.12,0:52:25.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:25.68,0:52:27.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,It generates the most tokens per watt.\N它每瓦特产生的词元数量最多。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:27.92,0:52:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:28.60,0:52:39.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so if the world's if the world's amount of watt power energy reduces it shifts their choices to the most productive version.\N所以如果全球的电力供应减少，人们就会转向最高效的版本。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:39.43,0:52:41.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is that they still want to make the revenues.\N原因在于他们仍希望实现收入目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:41.80,0:52:42.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.16,0:52:42.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.88,0:52:45.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so all of my CEO colleagues,\N所以我所有的CEO同事，
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.69,0:52:51.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,they all want to think all have ex high expectations for revenues next year and people have you know, they need to deliver it.\N他们都对明年收入抱有极高期望，而人们也必须实现这些目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.23,0:52:53.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Their shareholders counting on them to deliver it.\N他们的股东正指望他们实现目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.16,0:52:55.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,All their partners needed need them to deliver it.\N所有合作伙伴也都依赖他们实现目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:55.72,0:53:03.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so when the amount of power reduces, the quality of the compute you put into it has to has to be the most most extraordinary.\N因此当电力减少时，你投入其中的计算能力必须达到最卓越的水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:03.64,0:53:06.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're the most productive computing resource you could put in the world today.\N我们是当今世界上最具生产力的计算资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.74,0:53:08.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're the most rentable.\N我们也是最具可租赁性的。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.08,0:53:08.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.80,0:53:11.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're fungible and we're durable.\N我们是可替代的，也是持久的。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:11.62,0:53:23.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so the the the the forces around the world because of the shortage of resources is is shifting interest towards us.\N因此，由于全球资源短缺，各国的注意力正逐渐转向我们。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:23.29,0:53:25.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our market share was already very high.\N我们的市场份额已经非常高。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.36,0:53:25.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:26.04,0:53:29.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,But surprisingly to everybody, not only are we a large company and our market share is high,\N但令人惊讶的是，不仅我们是一家大型公司，市场份额也高，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.55,0:53:32.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,our market share is actually increasing for these reasons.\N我们的市场份额实际上正因这些原因而持续增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.20,0:53:32.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.84,0:53:38.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so you you you're going to see us go from and because we offer so much more per gigawatt than we used to,\N所以你们会看到，由于我们每吉瓦提供的能力远超以往，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:38.77,0:53:42.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,we used to be a GPU company then we became the largest and fastest growing networking company.\N我们曾是一家GPU公司，后来成为最大且增长最快的网络公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:42.84,0:53:47.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're now going to be one of the largest CPU companies, surely the fastest growing one.\N现在我们将成为最大的CPU公司之一，毫无疑问也是增长最快的。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:47.36,0:53:53.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So, because we're offering more and more and and we're in the you know, we're in computing for storage,\N所以，因为我们提供的越来越多，而且我们正处于计算与存储的交汇点，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:53.22,0:54:00.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're in computing for the knowledge infrastructure and so the amount of and now we're in security with Open Shell and Century.\N我们正致力于知识基础设施的计算，因此我们现在也进入了安全领域，\N推出了 Open Shell 和 Century。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:00.94,0:54:09.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so the the the offering that we we offer into 1 gigawatt went from went from uh uh I guess about,\N我们提供的 1 吉瓦算力的报价，从之前大约，
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.39,0:54:15.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, 18 billion or so per gigawatt to 20 somewhat billion per gigawatt to now 40 plus per gigawatt.\N每吉瓦 180 亿左右，上升到每吉瓦约 200 亿，现在已达到每吉瓦 400 亿以上。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:15.65,0:54:18.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And my sense is that that's going to keep on going up.\N我的感觉是，这个趋势还会持续上升。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.67,0:54:24.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so not only are we are we growing share because because people are shifting towards our computing platform,\N因此，我们不仅因为人们转向我们的计算平台而扩大市场份额，
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.61,0:54:28.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're also growing share because we offer more to the world's CapEx.\N还因为我们在全球资本开支中提供了更多价值而持续增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:28.28,0:54:33.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and to the to the world's a dollar dollar share of the market.\N以及在全球市场美元份额中的占比也在提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.09,0:54:33.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.56,0:54:33.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:34.04,0:54:34.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:34.32,0:54:38.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you look at if you look at just go back in just uh 6 years ago.\N如果你回溯一下，仅仅六年前的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:38.44,0:54:39.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.40,0:54:42.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Our percentage of the world's CapEx was in single digits.\N我们在全球资本开支中的占比还不到两位数。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:42.60,0:54:43.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:43.84,0:54:49.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um then I think I think right now with the world's CSPs we're probably running about 40%.\N嗯，我认为目前在云服务商中，我们的占比大概在40%左右。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:49.48,0:54:50.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:50.28,0:54:53.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we're also expanding the market beyond the the CSPs.\N但我们也正在将市场拓展到云服务商之外。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:53.72,0:54:59.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And outside of the CSPs, whether it's on prem or uh neo clouds Yeah.\N无论是本地部署还是新云厂商，都是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:59.08,0:55:03.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,half of our business our percentage of CapEx is probably what, 80%?\N我们一半的业务，资本开支占比可能达到了80%？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.12,0:55:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.84,0:55:06.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so And so between Yeah.\N所以，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:06.28,0:55:06.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:06.84,0:55:08.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,half of our business being 40%,\N一半的业务占40%，
Dialogue: 0,0:55:08.76,0:55:14.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,half of our business being 80% and both of us growing doubling every year and\N一半的业务占80%，而且两者每年都在翻倍增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.84,0:55:18.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,so you could see that our percentage of the world's CapEx is in fact even growing.\N所以你可以看到，我们占全球资本开支的比例实际上还在持续增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:19.04,0:55:19.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:19.44,0:55:28.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, one of those one of those buyers of Nvidia um is somebody we talked about 2 years ago, Elon, um when he started building Colossus.\N其中一位英伟达的买家，就是我们两年前谈过的人，埃隆，当时他开始建造“科洛斯”。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.55,0:55:36.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we were blown away a couple years ago to see him stand up a couple hundred thousand Hoppers right in Memphis.\N几年前我们看到他在孟菲斯直接部署了数以十万计的Hopper，真是震惊不已。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.20,0:55:39.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and I remember you saying nobody can do it like him.\N我还记得你说过，没人能像他这样干。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:39.30,0:55:45.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now he's raising another 40 billion, going to buy maybe million plus Vera Rubin's.\N现在他又要再融资400亿美元，计划购买超过百万台Vera Rubin。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:45.11,0:55:48.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, he's He's moved from the case to the end.\N他已从最初的机箱阶段，直接跃升到了终端部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.64,0:55:51.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,He says he wants to have 10 gigawatts by the end of 2027.\N他表示希望到2027年底实现10吉瓦的算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.03,0:55:56.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's hundreds of billions, right, spent on Vera Rubin.\N这意味着将投入数百亿美元用于Vera Rubin，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:56.88,0:55:59.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's an unprecedented rapid scale.\N这是前所未有的快速扩张。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:59.14,0:56:03.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,You were with him again yesterday when he was also presented with a medal.\N昨天你和他在一起，他还被授予了一枚奖章。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:03.89,0:56:09.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is Elon that much better at building compute today as he was then?\N埃隆现在构建算力的能力，真的比以前强这么多吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:09.10,0:56:10.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is it now obvious to you?\N现在你明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:10.81,0:56:17.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is it Is it a foregone conclusion that SpaceX will be the largest AI hyperscaler in the world?\N显然，SpaceX 将成为全球最大的 AI 超大规模云厂商，这已经成了定局吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:17.84,0:56:25.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we we we used to, you know, in the in the two parts of our chart, um, Elon used to be under enterprise.\N以前，在我们的图表的两个部分中，埃隆曾被归入企业类别。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:25.70,0:56:27.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's the way we reported our numbers.\N这就是我们报告数据的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.55,0:56:29.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now he's part of our CSPs.\N现在他属于我们的云服务商（CSPs）。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:29.32,0:56:29.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course.\N当然。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:29.80,0:56:30.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah.\N对，对。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:30.24,0:56:30.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Of course.\N当然。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:30.60,0:56:31.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so They're massive.\N所以他们规模巨大。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.52,0:56:37.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I'm I'm delighted that that that, um, uh, I love working with Elon.\N我很高兴能和埃隆一起工作，真的。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.22,0:56:45.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, he's using our technology for his own AI, um, in training models and such, uh, deploying models, of course.\N他正在使用我们的技术，用于自己的 AI 模型训练和部署。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:45.23,0:56:46.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Grokbot is super cool.\NGrokbot 非常酷。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:46.77,0:56:52.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and, um, uh, and the and the demand for Grokbot, the consumption for Grokbot is really skyrocketing.\N而且，呃，Groqbot的需求和使用量正在急剧飙升。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.73,0:56:54.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, of course, he rents it.\N然后，当然，他会租用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:54.44,0:56:54.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:54.76,0:56:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the combination of these three things he's fairly unique in doing that.\N所以这三件事的结合，让他在这一点上相当独特。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:58.92,0:57:02.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, I guess I guess, uh, uh, Google does that, right?\N嗯，我想，呃，谷歌也是这么做的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:02.28,0:57:05.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,That would be another yet another example.\N那又是一个例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:05.08,0:57:09.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I think he's he's, um, uh, also has the has the, uh,\N所以我认为他，呃，呃，还具备，
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.52,0:57:15.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,advantage that that he loves the intersection between computing and the physical build-outs.\N他对计算与物理基础设施建设交汇点的热爱这一优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:15.80,0:57:16.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:16.24,0:57:18.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, he loves that that whole area.\N他真的很喜欢这个领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:18.36,0:57:21.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And nobody knows more about energy than he does.\N没有人比他更懂能源了。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:21.08,0:57:27.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and and, uh, one particular, uh, new market that we're going to go explore together is putting data centers out in space.\N而且，呃，我们即将共同探索的一个新市场是，把数据中心放到太空中。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:27.14,0:57:32.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so our two engineering teams are working super closely together, uh, to create a a new type of server,\N因此我们的两个工程团队正紧密合作，共同打造一种新型服务器，
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.50,0:57:38.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,a new type of architecture, um, that might might, uh, be super good, you know, you know, in space and on Earth.\N一种新型架构，这种架构可能在太空和地球上都表现得非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.84,0:57:42.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we saw that Starship launched last week, you know,\N我们看到星舰上周发射了，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:57:42.15,0:57:46.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,had its its its first orbital rendezvous and was launching those V3 sats\N完成了首次轨道交会，并发射了那些V3卫星，
Dialogue: 0,0:57:46.92,0:57:51.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,that literally captured the imagination and kind of broke Twitter for a moment.\N这些场景简直激发了人们的想象力，甚至让推特短暂瘫痪。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:51.67,0:57:54.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just people mesmerized by watching these launch into space.\N只是人们被这些飞船升空的景象深深吸引。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:54.72,0:57:56.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can't wait to be a payload.\N我迫不及待想成为其中的载荷。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:56.08,0:57:57.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Me not personally.\N我个人可不想。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:57.48,0:58:05.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you think Does that get Do you have increasing confidence that we will have a material amount of compute in space,\N你是否越来越有信心，认为我们到2028年、2029年左右，能通过星舰实现大量太空算力，
Dialogue: 0,0:58:05.28,0:58:08.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, via via Starship by let's call it 2028, 2029?\N你知道，到那时我们能在太空中实现实质性的算力部署？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:08.68,0:58:17.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, Elon's put some big numbers out there, but do you think that we can get to material inference in space in that in that time frame?\N埃隆确实提出了不少大数字，但你认为我们真能在那个时间框架内实现太空中的实质性推理能力吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:17.12,0:58:18.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Only Nvidia compute.\N只有英伟达的算力。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:18.83,0:58:20.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And let let me tell you why.\N而且让我告诉你原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:20.37,0:58:22.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not not just about the technology.\N这不仅仅关乎技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:22.88,0:58:26.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nvidia's performance per unit energy is the world's best.\N英伟达单位能耗的性能是全球最佳。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.76,0:58:31.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we call it performance watt, and but the most important thing is is this.\N因此我们称之为性能瓦特，但最重要的是这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:31.28,0:58:37.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,The productivity of Nvidia's compute is so good, meaning the return on investment invested capital is so good.\N英伟达计算的生产效率极高，意味着投资资本的回报率非常可观。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:38.04,0:58:39.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:39.16,0:58:44.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,That you could put it out in space, and the launch costs is a small percentage of it.\N你甚至可以把它放到太空中，发射成本仅占其价值的一小部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:44.76,0:58:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:45.88,0:58:50.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,The launch cost is not inconsequential, and so, you're not going to put low-cost computing out there.\N发射成本并非微不足道，因此你不会把低成本计算设备送入太空。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:50.62,0:58:53.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're going to put high-value computing out there.\N你会把高价值计算设备送入太空。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:53.12,0:59:00.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we're the highest-value computing system you could imagine, the highest computing system in the history of computing.\N所以，我们是你可以想象到的最高价值计算系统，是计算史上最高性能的计算系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.16,0:59:08.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we're the perfect fit, really, to launch into space right now, irrespective of the the launch cost, it'll still be excellent ROI.\N因此，我们非常适合现在就发射到太空，无论发射成本如何，其投资回报率依然非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:08.36,0:59:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, do we get 500 megawatts in space by '29?\N那么，我们能在2029年之前实现500兆瓦的太空发电吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.20,0:59:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, I'll I'll let him let him tell you, but but, um, I I think I I You know,\N呃，我让他来告诉你吧，不过，呃，我觉得……你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:59:17.68,0:59:21.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,what what's Elon's what launching a a hundred launches a year right now?\N埃隆现在每年发射一百次，这到底意味着什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:21.98,0:59:24.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know what exactly it is, but it's a lot. a day.\N我不太清楚具体是多少，但数量非常大，每天都有。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:24.60,0:59:25.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, right.\N是的，没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:25.48,0:59:29.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, uh, you could you could put Vera Rubin in there and and I'll justify it.\N所以，呃，你可以把维拉·鲁宾放进去，我来为它辩护。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:29.99,0:59:32.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,The demand demand is there.\N需求确实存在。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:32.12,0:59:34.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,His return on investment is so good on it.\N他的投资回报率非常高。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:34.15,0:59:36.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the productivity is excellent.\N因此生产效率非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:36.59,0:59:39.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's fungible meaning you put a satellite on space.\N它具有可替代性，意味着你把一颗卫星送上太空。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.19,0:59:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you don't have a customer to will rent it, it sits idle and you certainly don't want that.\N如果没有客户租用它，它就会闲置，这显然不是你想要的。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:43.52,0:59:48.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So when we do compute it's going to be fully fungible and there'll be lots and lots of renters.\N所以当我们进行计算时，它将是完全可替代的，会有大量租户。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:48.94,0:59:52.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know we have we work with every single closed model company in the world.\N你知道，我们与世界上每一家闭源模型公司都有合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:52.88,0:59:55.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,We run every single open model in the world.\N我们运行着世界上每一个开源模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:55.34,0:59:57.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have thousands of startups working with us.\N我们有数千家初创公司与我们合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:57.84,1:00:00.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so and enterprises around in every single industry.\N以及遍布各个行业的各类企业。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:00.60,1:00:04.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so the computing is completely fungible and is durable.\N因此，计算资源完全可互换且持久耐用。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:04.20,1:00:04.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:04.60,1:00:10.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, it'll last it'll sit up there and we'll keep up and the reason for that is because we keep CUDA upgrading the software.\N你知道，它会一直待在那儿，我们会持续更新，原因在于我们不断升级 CUDA 软件。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:10.26,1:00:18.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know we're the only com- hardware company in the world that you pay us 8 years ago and we're still updating your software new algorithms.\N你知道，我们是全球唯一一家硬件公司，即使你八年前购买了我们的产品，我们仍在持续为你更新软件和新算法。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:18.48,1:00:18.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:18.84,1:00:23.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, and so we'll we'll update the software for as long as the satellite's up there.\N所以，只要卫星还在天上，我们就会持续更新软件。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:23.28,1:00:25.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so it's going to be really durable.\N因此，它的耐用性将非常强。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:25.67,1:00:28.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I I think the combination of these three traits Yes.\N所以我认为，这三种特质的结合非常关键。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:29.00,1:00:33.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,along with the technology makes it the perfect payload for for a SpaceX.\N随着这项技术的发展，它成为太空探索公司（SpaceX）的理想载荷。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:33.84,1:00:37.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um It costs trillions of dollars to build all this CapEx.\N建造这些设施需要数万亿美元的资本开支。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:37.64,1:00:42.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,You guys have leveraged your own balance sheet to help folks like the Neo clouds build that out.\N你们利用自身资产负债表，帮助像新云厂商这样的公司完成建设。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:42.60,1:00:46.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,In order for finance people to get it to pencil out they need to see payback, right?\N为了让财务人员觉得这笔投资划算，他们需要看到回报，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:46.97,1:00:51.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um You talked about you know some companies seeing one year payback, right?\N你们提到有些公司一年就能收回成本，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:51.47,1:00:57.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,50 billion dollars in the first year, you know, some some spot price seen out of out of SpaceX perhaps.\N第一年就达到500亿美元，可能来自太空探索公司（SpaceX）的某些现货价格。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:57.58,1:01:00.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but if I look at the total incremental off-take, right?\N但如果我来看总的增量需求，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:00.64,1:01:03.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,The revenue of all the labs this year.\N今年所有实验室的收入。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:03.05,1:01:05.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if I add up, you know, the two frontier labs.\N所以如果我把两个前沿实验室的收入加起来。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:05.56,1:01:07.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah, get yourself a snack.\N哦，顺便给自己来点零食。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:07.17,1:01:12.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we add up, you know, some of the inference labs, it's about 200 billion dollars, okay?\N再加上一些推理实验室的收入，大约是2000亿美元，明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:13.00,1:01:16.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um We need to see that double next year to 400 billion.\N我们明年需要看到这个数字翻倍，达到4000亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:16.44,1:01:20.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need to see it double the year after that to 800 billion, right?\N我们需要看到它在下一年翻倍，达到8000亿美元，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:20.72,1:01:26.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,In order to get in the zip code of the payback on trillions of dollars of CapEx.\N为了实现对数万亿美元资本开支的回报。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:26.60,1:01:34.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we had this massive unlock this year with with Claude code that led to a 10x increase in Anthropic's revenues.\N今年我们通过 Claude Code 实现了巨大的突破，使 Anthropic 的收入增长了10倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:34.72,1:01:41.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's your confidence that the labs can continue to two to three x their revenues every year in order that\N你有多大把握，这些实验室能持续实现每年两到三倍的收入增长？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:41.97,1:01:50.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,we get the payback that's going to be required just to to to build out trillions of dollars of CapEx.\N以确保我们获得回报，而这回报正是建设数万亿美元资本开支所必需的。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:50.16,1:01:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, you're investing in these companies.\N你实际上是在投资这些公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.72,1:01:54.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have a you have big investments in these companies, right?\N你对这些公司有巨额投资，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:54.60,1:01:57.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you see that level of growth continuing in these companies?\N你认为这些公司的这种增长水平会持续下去吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:58.04,1:01:58.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah.\N当然。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:58.49,1:02:01.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,People misunderstand what's going on.\N人们误解了正在发生的事情。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:01.52,1:02:09.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, first of all particularly I mean Nvidia represents call it 80% of the revenue share of AI infrastructure in the market today.\N首先，特别是英伟达目前代表了人工智能基础设施市场约80%的收入份额。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:09.70,1:02:18.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it's And so my description of of the universe of computing Nvidia computing matters here.\N因此，英伟达计算在计算宇宙中的重要性就显得尤为关键。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:18.12,1:02:21.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,There really basically call it three segments.\N其实基本上可以分为三个部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:21.12,1:02:22.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Three large segments.\N三个大的部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:22.22,1:02:26.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's It's probably slightly more than that, but let me just kind of categorize them in three large segments.\N可能略多于三个，但我就大致分为三个大的部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:26.34,1:02:29.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first segment of our computing is just baseline computing.\N我们计算的第一部分是基础计算。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:29.68,1:02:35.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just meaning you use it for data processing, molecular dynamics, physics simulation,\N也就是用于数据处理、分子动力学、物理模拟，
Dialogue: 0,1:02:35.73,1:02:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,um fusion simulation, fusion simulation, you know, you name it, right?\N比如核聚变模拟，核聚变模拟，你随便说，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:02:40.32,1:02:43.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Quantum chemistry, quantum physics, you know, and so everything.\N量子化学、量子物理，等等，所有这些。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:43.72,1:02:44.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:44.20,1:02:44.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:02:44.50,1:02:48.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,The world of simulation and data processing, not to mention computer graphics.\N模拟与数据处理的世界，更不用说计算机图形学了。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:48.48,1:02:56.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so all of that processing done on our GPUs If you just kind of said there was no AI at all, just classical machine learning,\N所有这些处理都是在我们的 GPU 上完成的，如果你说完全没有 AI，只有传统机器学习，
Dialogue: 0,1:02:56.97,1:03:05.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,XGBoost at Visa, My MasterCard, you know, for fraud detection, our recommender systems to figure out what news to recommend to you.\N比如 Visa 的 XGBoost，MasterCard 的模型，用于欺诈检测，\N我们的推荐系统来判断该给你推荐什么新闻。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:05.15,1:03:13.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,You just all of that stuff combined classical computing, not AI, not deep learning, not agentic systems, I'm going to call it a third of our business.\N你刚才提到的那些东西，结合了传统计算，不是AI，不是深度学习，\N也不是代理式系统，我把它称为我们业务的三分之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:13.20,1:03:14.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:14.32,1:03:19.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that business is growing, you know, call it 30% 40% per year.\N而这部分业务正在增长，可以说每年增长30%到40%。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.44,1:03:19.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:20.00,1:03:20.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:03:20.42,1:03:23.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the absence of any AI labs, Nvidia's not zero, right?\N没有AI实验室的情况下，英伟达的业务也不是零，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:03:23.79,1:03:25.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're we're quite a large company.\N我们是一家相当大的公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:25.88,1:03:27.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, so that's number one.\N所以这是第一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:27.09,1:03:35.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second part is um the AI labs people see two but we work with every one of them.\N第二部分是，人们看到的是AI实验室，但我们和每一个都在合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:35.96,1:03:36.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:36.36,1:03:39.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh Meta Muse is doing fantastic, right?\N而且Meta Muse的表现非常出色，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:03:39.44,1:03:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Incredible.\N太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:40.08,1:03:44.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's vastly Nvidia and and you know they were zero last year.\N而且这几乎完全依赖英伟达，你知道的，他们去年还是一片空白。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:44.84,1:03:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:45.52,1:03:51.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, or a year before that they were just recommender systems and now they're, you know killing it with Meta Muse.\N你知道，再往前一年，他们还只是推荐系统，现在却用 Meta Muse 大获成功。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:52.04,1:03:56.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um of course Grok Mhm. didn't exist 3 years ago.\N还有，Grok，嗯，三年前还不存在。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:56.64,1:04:00.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we didn't run Gemini uh before we run Gemini now.\N嗯，我们之前没运行过 Gemini，现在才开始用。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:00.52,1:04:04.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and uh starting this year we started working with Anthropic.\N嗯，从今年开始，我们开始和 Anthropic 合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:04.48,1:04:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so if you just kind of look at our compute, people see a couple of labs but I see more than that.\N所以如果你大致看看我们的计算资源，人们只看到几个实验室，而我看到的远不止这些。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:10.44,1:04:12.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,I see five, six labs, okay?\N我看到了五个、六个实验室，明白吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:04:12.87,1:04:14.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so these labs are all doing great.\N所以这些实验室都做得非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:15.04,1:04:15.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Correct.\N正确。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:15.72,1:04:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and if you if you told me that that represents um not quite 1/3 of our business, let's say a quarter of our compute Mhm. fantastic.\N如果你告诉我，这还不到我们业务的三分之一，大概只占我们计算资源的四分之一，嗯，那太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:26.28,1:04:26.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:04:26.84,1:04:29.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's say that's a quarter.\N所以我们假设这是四分之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:29.72,1:04:36.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when people are looking at 80 Nvidia and and we now run the infrastructure of the world and I just said 25% of it,\N当人们看到英伟达的80%时，我们实际上正在运行全球的基础设施，我刚才说其中25%是这样。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:36.93,1:04:39.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,maybe 30% of it is the frontier labs.\N或许有30%属于前沿实验室。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:39.88,1:04:41.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:41.16,1:04:45.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you know, call it a third is um uh just processing in general.\N嗯，可以说三分之一是通用处理。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.84,1:04:46.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:46.52,1:04:50.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And another third, this is the the the part that's really great.\N而另外三分之一，这部分才是真正精彩的地方。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:50.20,1:04:58.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um because we're at the beginning of a new computing platform shift just a vast number of new startups that are coming out.\N因为我们正处于新一轮计算平台转型的起点，大量新创公司正涌现出来。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:58.86,1:05:00.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So many great companies.\N这里有太多优秀的企业。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:00.64,1:05:06.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,And some of them are of course doing consumer stuff, you know, uh one of them really doing great, Noah Instinct.\N其中一些当然在做消费级产品，比如诺亚本能，表现非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:06.31,1:05:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was just going to mention that.\N我正想提到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:07.76,1:05:15.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and Noah's doing great um too uh all kinds of physical AI, biological AI, uh, material sciences AI,\N没错，诺亚也在做得很好，涵盖了各种物理AI、生物AI以及材料科学AI。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:15.90,1:05:20.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh, uh, Jeff's Jeff Bezos' new company Prometheus, uh, they're doing they're doing fantastic.\N嗯，杰夫·贝索斯的新公司普罗米修斯，他们做得非常出色。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:20.77,1:05:27.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the the number of companies across the spectrum of industries that have been started, thousands of them.\N因此，从各个行业涌现出来的初创公司数量，成千上万。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:27.69,1:05:28.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what do they do?\N那他们做什么呢？
Dialogue: 0,1:05:28.76,1:05:30.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,They rent Nvidia computers.\N他们租用英伟达的计算机。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:30.24,1:05:31.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, they're renters.\N所以，他们是租户。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:31.46,1:05:38.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, what is a third of our business is kind of cloud computing for the next generation.\N因此，我们业务的三分之一，相当于下一代的云计算。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:38.70,1:05:39.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:39.18,1:05:41.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's kind of like AWS for today, you know?\N就像今天的 AWS 一样，你知道吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:05:41.89,1:05:44.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, it's just not AWS for the future.\N但这不仅仅是未来的 AWS。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:44.56,1:05:45.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:45.28,1:05:49.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that represents about a third of our business altogether, you know?\N这大约占我们整体业务的三分之一，你知道吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:05:49.06,1:05:56.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, my sense is that this we're in the early innings of the build-out of this new computing architecture.\N我的感觉是，我们正处在构建这一新计算架构的早期阶段。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:56.16,1:06:04.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, um, I it's it's a very it's it's a real big mistake to recognize just a couple of companies and think that they were funding the infrastructure.\N而且，呃，认为只要关注少数几家公司，就觉得它们在资助基础设施，这是一个非常严重的错误。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:04.32,1:06:07.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, one observation, uh, open models.\N然后，有一个观察，呃，开源模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:07.91,1:06:10.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,You you know that that I I've been a great advocate of open models.\N你知道，我一直都是开源模型的坚定倡导者。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:10.74,1:06:14.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because open models opens up new opportunities.\N这样做的原因在于，开源模型打开了新的机遇。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:14.66,1:06:17.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you look at all these startup companies, 80% of them use open models.\N如果你看看这些初创公司，80%都在使用开源模型。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:17.92,1:06:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:18.64,1:06:22.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and they're not using it to compete with the frontier labs.\N他们并不是用这些模型去跟前沿实验室竞争。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:22.19,1:06:25.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're using it to unlock a new opportunity somewhere else.\N他们是在用这些模型，去开拓其他领域的全新机会。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:25.68,1:06:28.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, it could be in physical AI, could be manufacturing, could be health care.\N比如物理 AI，比如制造，比如医疗健康。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:28.62,1:06:31.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're doing something completely completely different.\N他们做的事完全是完全不同的。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:31.44,1:06:31.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:31.72,1:06:36.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and they're taking, um, these open models and and many of them taking Nemotron.\N而且他们正在使用这些开源模型，其中很多人还在使用 Nemotron。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:36.71,1:06:41.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the these models are then customized into super intelligence.\N然后这些模型会被定制为超级智能。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:41.72,1:06:42.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:42.56,1:06:49.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, if you will, I kind of see that the the the general the general closed labs will be artificial general intelligence.\N所以，如果你愿意的话，我觉得通用封闭实验室将实现人工通用智能。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:49.58,1:06:50.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it gets super good.\N它变得极其出色。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:50.72,1:06:51.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:51.16,1:06:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, you have all these vertical companies that are focused on a particular domain, and they have very proprietary data.\N然后你还会看到许多专注于特定领域的垂直公司，它们拥有非常专有的数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:57.20,1:06:59.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,They teach it to do something very specific.\N它们教会模型完成某项非常具体的任务。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:59.56,1:07:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And they achieve super intelligence for their domain.\N它们在各自领域实现了超级智能。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:02.00,1:07:02.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:02.48,1:07:07.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you don't see, you know, so again, um, if if we go to your compute math,\N所以，你不会看到，你知道，再次强调，如果我们回到你的计算数学，
Dialogue: 0,1:07:07.50,1:07:14.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,which I think a lot of people are using to forecast the future revenues of of of the labs, for example.\N我认为很多人正用它来预测实验室的未来收入，比如。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:14.38,1:07:20.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, you said, "Hey, if you stand up a gigawatt of this compute, you can get, you know, 40, 50 billion dollars out the other end."\N你知道，你说过，“如果你部署一吉瓦的这种算力，另一端就能产出大约400亿到500亿美元。”
Dialogue: 0,1:07:20.29,1:07:25.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if we took the number we talked about earlier, 40 gigawatts of compute coming online next year,\N但如果我们采用之前提到的数字，即明年将有40吉瓦的算力上线，
Dialogue: 0,1:07:25.58,1:07:33.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,and if you took 40 billion out the other end, then that would be 1.6 trillion of revenues coming out the other end of that factory.\N然后你从另一端拿出400亿，那么从这个工厂另一端出来的收入将达到1.6万亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:33.32,1:07:37.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,But of course, there's something, you know, it it doesn't work that way, right?\N但当然，其实不是这样的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:37.74,1:07:42.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the end of the day, there's you got to look at the demand curve and the rate of diffusion to determine,\N归根结底，你必须看需求曲线和扩散速率来判断，
Dialogue: 0,1:07:42.71,1:07:45.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,right, the revenue that's going to come out the other end of the factory.\N从工厂另一端出来的收入会是多少。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:45.83,1:07:49.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what I hear a lot is that people are nervous, right?\N我听到很多人说，他们感到担忧，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:49.60,1:07:53.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,They've seen over the course of the year, maybe the labs revenue slowing down a little bit,\N他们看到今年实验室的收入略有放缓，
Dialogue: 0,1:07:53.89,1:07:59.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,and they're nervous that, you know, at some point you're going to have the proverbial bubble popping, right?\N于是担心，总有一天会出现所谓的泡沫破裂，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:59.43,1:08:03.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where we have more supply coming online than we have demand at a moment in time.\N那就是说，算力的供应增长超过了当前的需求。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:04.01,1:08:09.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,That AI is more like these step functions rather than just this parabolic line straight up.\N这种AI更像是阶梯式增长，而不是一条平滑向上的抛物线。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:09.16,1:08:12.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,I guess the question to you is, do are you worried about, you know,\N我想问你的是，你是否担心，
Dialogue: 0,1:08:12.62,1:08:18.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,a moment in time where everybody gets nervous about financing the build-out, right?\N会出现一个所有人都对融资建设感到焦虑的时刻，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:08:18.54,1:08:21.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um and then we don't get the build-out.\N而且我们得不到建设投入。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:22.00,1:08:25.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, you know, all these different things you just got to break it down.\N嗯，你知道，所有这些不同的东西，你得把它拆解开来。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:25.16,1:08:32.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Break it down back down to first principles and and um Uh the the part that people are trying to extrapolate\N拆解到最基本的原理，然后嗯，人们试图推断的部分，
Dialogue: 0,1:08:32.06,1:08:38.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,the 100 100 100 billion dollars of ARR or 25 billion dollars of ARR they're trying to extrapolate is a small part,\N比如 1000 亿美元的年经常性收入或 250 亿美元的年经常性收入，\N他们试图推断的只是其中一小部分，
Dialogue: 0,1:08:38.95,1:08:42.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,not a small part, it's it's just a part Right.\N不是小部分，它只是整体建设投入中的一小部分，没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:42.40,1:08:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,of the overall infrastructure build-out.\N的整体基础设施建设投入。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:44.16,1:08:44.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,For sure.\N绝对是。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:44.52,1:08:48.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so so the question is, are people going to continue doing shopping online?\N所以问题来了，人们还会继续在线购物吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:08:48.48,1:08:48.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:48.84,1:08:49.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know.\N你知道。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:49.20,1:08:49.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:49.56,1:08:52.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's So that third of the build-out, let's call that a third.\N那么，这部分建设投入，我们姑且称之为三分之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:52.62,1:08:54.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You said it's 30 of this.\N你说的是这个的30%。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:54.52,1:08:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take that to the bank.\N这话可以当真。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:55.68,1:08:55.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:55.92,1:08:56.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:08:56.15,1:08:57.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,That that like that's not even a debate.\N那根本就不是个争论。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:57.50,1:08:58.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a third of the build-out is going to come out.\N所以，建设规模的三分之一将被释放出来。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:59.04,1:08:59.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know,\N你知道，
Dialogue: 0,1:08:59.75,1:09:03.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,I said I said a few couple Was it a couple years ago that as we\N我说过——就几年前——当我们
Dialogue: 0,1:09:03.77,1:09:10.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,exit this decade infrastructure build out will probably somewhere between three to four trillion a year.\N走出这个十年时，每年基础设施建设大概在三万亿到四万亿之间。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:10.17,1:09:17.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, you know, obviously it's closer to four than it is closer to three and and um per year per year yeah by the end of the decade Yeah,\N嗯，显然更接近四万亿而不是三万亿——每年，到本十年末。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:17.86,1:09:22.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,and if you if you said if you said that one and a half trillion of that was just compute.\N而且如果你说其中有一点五万亿只是算力。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:22.72,1:09:23.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:23.30,1:09:23.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:23.88,1:09:24.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just compute.\N只需计算。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:24.52,1:09:26.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, why is it going to be so big?\N现在，为什么它会变得如此巨大？
Dialogue: 0,1:09:26.96,1:09:30.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, it was half a trillion before I started.\N好吧，我开始之前它就已经是五千亿了。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:30.12,1:09:31.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:31.96,1:09:34.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if I told you that over the course of some six, seven,\N如果我告诉你，在大约六到七，
Dialogue: 0,1:09:35.03,1:09:39.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,eight years became one and a half trillion because the world is just consuming more compute.\N八年的时间里，它增长到了一千五百亿，因为全世界对计算的需求正在增加。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:39.32,1:09:39.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:39.72,1:09:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, that's not illogical.\N这并不荒谬。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.00,1:09:41.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.80,1:09:46.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,On top of this, remember um Moore's law is over.\N此外，记住，摩尔定律已经失效了。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:46.56,1:09:47.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:47.16,1:09:51.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,There was a time if you want to get twice as many transistors, you just wait one year.\N曾经，如果你想让晶体管数量翻倍，只需等一年即可。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:51.52,1:09:51.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:52.04,1:09:55.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you want twice as many transistors get another wait one year, same price.\N如果你想让晶体管数量翻倍，再等一年，价格也一样。
Dialogue: 0,1:09:55.72,1:10:00.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if you want twice as many transistors now, doesn't matter how long you wait, you have to pay twice as much.\N但如今，无论你等多久，想要晶体管数量翻倍，都得付出双倍的代价。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:00.56,1:10:02.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, because Moore's law is over.\N好吧，因为摩尔定律已经失效了。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:02.32,1:10:08.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, whatever whatever computing capacity that the world wants Right.\N所以，无论世界需要多少计算能力，
Dialogue: 0,1:10:08.32,1:10:11.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,every single year if you want twice as much you're going to pay twice as much.\N每年如果想要翻倍，就得付出双倍的费用。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:11.56,1:10:12.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:12.28,1:10:17.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, on top of that half a trillion dollars that was kind of growing just naturally Right.\N在原本自然增长的五千亿美金基础上，
Dialogue: 0,1:10:17.92,1:10:25.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,because the world just use more and more digital you're going to have to effectively you know, given an X factor Yeah.\N因为世界越来越依赖数字化，你实际上必须额外考虑一个X倍的因素。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:25.52,1:10:27.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,just to account for the fact that Moore's law is over.\N仅仅是为了应对摩尔定律的终结。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:27.96,1:10:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:28.60,1:10:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, without AI Mhm.\N所以，没有 AI 的话，嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:31.20,1:10:34.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,the semiconductor industry was on its path to become the largest industry in the world.\N半导体行业正走上成为全球最大产业的道路。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:34.92,1:10:35.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:35.28,1:10:37.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I've mentioned that long ago just people forgot.\N我之前就提过，只是人们忘了。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:38.00,1:10:39.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was just one of those things that I said.\N那只是我随口说的一件事。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:39.68,1:10:40.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes, yes, yes, yes.\N对，对，对，对。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:40.80,1:10:42.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I just said that two years ago, yeah.\N我两年前就说过这话，没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:42.08,1:10:42.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:42.56,1:10:43.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:43.16,1:10:44.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so so that's just one part.\N所以，这只是其中一部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:45.04,1:10:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:45.52,1:10:45.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so,\N所以，
Dialogue: 0,1:10:45.87,1:10:53.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the only thing that we and then and then don't forget because we're in the new computing platform shift there going to be a whole lot of startups.\N我们唯一要记住的是，由于我们正处于新的计算平台转型期，将会涌现出大量初创企业。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:53.80,1:10:54.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:53.96,1:10:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Innovation is part of the economy.\N创新是经济的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:56.20,1:10:56.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:57.00,1:10:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,New companies come it's accelerating.\N新公司不断涌现，速度正在加快。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:58.92,1:10:59.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:10:59.24,1:11:04.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,You you so if we spent if you go back to Moore's law, general purpose compute $5 billion per gigawatt.\N如果我们回顾摩尔定律，通用计算的成本是每吉瓦50亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:05.04,1:11:05.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:05.44,1:11:06.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today it's 50.\N如今这个数字是50。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:06.36,1:11:06.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:06.80,1:11:07.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:11:07.10,1:11:07.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,For Vera Rubin.\N针对维拉·鲁宾。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:07.79,1:11:12.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the question is is Vera Rubin deliver 10x more valuable in the world?\N所以问题在于，维拉·鲁宾能否为世界带来10倍的价值？
Dialogue: 0,1:11:12.72,1:11:18.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,The punchline is I don't think it's necessary to extrapolate any of the labs into multiple trillions of dollars.\N结论是，我认为没有必要将任何实验室的投入外推到数万亿美元的规模。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:18.16,1:11:18.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:18.41,1:11:19.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Unnecessary to do that.\N做这种外推是不必要的。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:19.40,1:11:19.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:19.65,1:11:25.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's a I mean it's an important one because I think people you know, we just saw yesterday you know,\N我认为这很重要，因为我想人们知道，我们昨天刚看到，
Dialogue: 0,1:11:25.51,1:11:31.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,even in the market you know, some chatter about was open AI's revenue 70 billion or 50 billion.\N即使在市场层面，也有关于OpenAI收入是700亿还是500亿的传闻。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:31.22,1:11:34.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think you and I They're going to be insanely successful companies.\N我认为你和我都很清楚，它们会是极其成功的企业。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:34.20,1:11:34.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Correct.\N正确。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:34.80,1:11:35.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:35.24,1:11:40.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you saw the pullback in a lot of the infrastructure companies right on the fear that oh\N但你看到了很多基础设施公司的回调，原因正是出于担忧，
Dialogue: 0,1:11:40.73,1:11:46.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,my gosh open AI doesn't have the money won't have the money in order to pay for the infrastructure.\N天啊，OpenAI没有钱了，无法支付基础设施的开销。
Dialogue: 0,1:11:46.06,1:11:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the point that you're hammering home is that when we look at the 40 gigawatts of infrastructure built out next year,\N我认为你反复强调的重点是，当我们展望明年建成的40吉瓦基础设施时，
Dialogue: 0,1:11:53.68,1:12:00.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,at least a third of it is just going to right general purpose compute replacement the the the basic stuff out of the hyperscalers.\N至少三分之一将用于替代超大规模云厂商的基础通用计算资源。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:00.89,1:12:07.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,That a third of it's going to kind of neo cloud sovereigns enterprises everybody else who's using this all the startups and a\N另三分之一将流向新兴的“新云厂商”、主权企业以及所有使用这些技术的初创公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:07.40,1:12:14.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,third of it's going to not two labs but to many labs right including Grok and thinking machines and all the other Yeah.\N剩下的三分之一将流向众多实验室，而不仅仅是两个实验室，包括Grok和思维机器等其他机构。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:14.58,1:12:14.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:14.79,1:12:16.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're putting way too much pressure on two labs.\N我们对这两个实验室施加了过大的压力。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:16.84,1:12:17.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:17.44,1:12:19.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm delighted to partner with them and and support them.\N我很高兴能与他们合作并支持他们。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:19.84,1:12:24.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh they're going to be uh two of the most consequential technology companies ever built in history.\N他们将成为历史上最具影响力的科技公司之一。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:24.57,1:12:27.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh they're going to be magnificently successful.\N他们必将取得辉煌的成功。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:27.36,1:12:27.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:27.88,1:12:32.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,But they don't have to be anywhere near a trillion dollars in revenues to be successful.\N但他们并不需要达到万亿收入规模才能成功。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:32.40,1:12:32.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:32.84,1:12:33.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:33.08,1:12:35.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we're putting way too much pressure on that and then the rest of\N我觉得我们对那件事施加了太多压力，然后整个行业也得承受。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:35.60,1:12:39.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,the industry we still do have to build out a few trillion dollars of computing infrastructure.\N我们仍然需要投入数万亿美元来建设计算基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:39.96,1:12:45.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um just to keep going um let's let's shift a little bit. is this you guys?\N嗯，继续说吧，我们稍微转换一下话题。这些是你们的吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:12:45.61,1:12:46.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Come on.\N来吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:46.16,1:12:48.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,By the way, what are what are these called?\N对了，这些叫什么来着？
Dialogue: 0,1:12:48.12,1:12:49.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are dried plums.\N这是李子干。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:49.68,1:12:50.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Dried plums.\N李子干。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:50.46,1:12:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,The old dried plums.\N以前的李子干。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:51.72,1:12:54.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,This one particular particular store in Taiwan is one of my favorites.\N台湾有家特别的店是我最喜欢的。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:55.00,1:12:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Kind of a licorice-y There is licorice.\N带点甘草味，确实有甘草。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:57.40,1:12:59.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and licorice, a little licorice-y.\N对，还有甘草，带点甘草味。
Dialogue: 0,1:12:59.68,1:13:01.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, salt, sugar, cinnamon.\N嗯，盐、糖、肉桂。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:01.56,1:13:01.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:01.82,1:13:02.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Has a little twang to it.\N有点酸味。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:02.96,1:13:04.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah, you got it.\N对，对，就是这个味。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:04.20,1:13:04.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know.\N你知道的。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:04.72,1:13:05.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:05.58,1:13:06.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:06.44,1:13:13.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,You said as to next year, demand for Nvidia's chips well over 100%.\N你说过明年英伟达芯片的需求将超过100%。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:13.40,1:13:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You guided to 70% revenue growth.\N你预测收入增长70%。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:15.48,1:13:20.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,You gave a a year forward look because you said supply is constrained.\N你给出了未来一年的展望，因为你提到供应受限。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:20.28,1:13:21.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's all I had at the time.\N那就是我当时想到的所有问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:21.36,1:13:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:21.96,1:13:22.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:22.32,1:13:23.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I got 18 months to work it.\N我还有18个月时间来搞定它。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:24.00,1:13:24.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:24.36,1:13:27.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,You said you were very confident I'll come to work every day.\N你说过你非常有信心，我会每天都来上班。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:27.72,1:13:32.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,You said very confident and plenty of time to work with the supply chain to do even better.\N你说过非常有信心，而且有充足时间与供应链协作，做得更好。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:32.76,1:13:36.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,You expected to do even better and then not disappoint customers.\N你预期能做得更好，然后不辜负客户。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:36.44,1:13:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, are are things going even better?\N那么，事情进展得是不是更好了？
Dialogue: 0,1:13:39.52,1:13:41.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And has the order book continued to grow?\N订单簿是否还在持续增长？
Dialogue: 0,1:13:41.29,1:13:44.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because the other part of that is, right, you took a snapshot at a moment time.\N因为那部分的另一面是，你当时只是在某个时间点做了个快照。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:44.50,1:13:47.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And of course, people are continuing, you know, to place orders.\N当然，人们仍在持续下单。
Dialogue: 0,1:13:47.32,1:13:51.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it Do you think there's enough slack in the supply chain you can squeeze more out?\N所以，你觉得供应链还有足够的弹性，能再挤出更多产能吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:13:51.44,1:14:01.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And is the order book continuing to grow as more of these capabilities are unlocked?\N随着这些能力不断解锁，订单量是否仍在持续增长？
Dialogue: 0,1:14:01.12,1:14:09.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,The First of all, let me tell you why I told everybody um The challenge that we have is we have giant order books.\N首先，让我告诉你们，我之所以告诉所有人，是因为我们面临的挑战是，我们手上有巨大的订单量。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:09.76,1:14:14.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single CSP, every single NCP, every single OEM had already placed orders on us.\N每一家云服务商、每一家网络服务提供商、每一家原始设备制造商都已向我们下了订单。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.38,1:14:18.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Startups, big company, small company, they already placed orders on us.\N初创公司、大公司、小公司，他们都已向我们下了订单。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:18.36,1:14:26.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because we work with them on a on a depending on on the size of the customer at least a year.\N原因在于，我们与客户合作的时间至少长达一年，具体取决于客户规模。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:26.48,1:14:29.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, for the the largest ones, 2 years forecast.\N对于最大的客户，我们甚至会提前两年进行预测。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:29.44,1:14:34.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so we already have a a very large order book.\N因此，我们已经拥有非常庞大的订单量。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:34.56,1:14:44.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And because I was in the process of allocating and what I was allocating to all of our customers is a lot less than they wanted. they wanted.\N而且，当我正在分配资源时，分配给所有客户的部分远少于他们期望的数量。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:44.80,1:14:45.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:45.96,1:14:52.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,If I if I was If I didn't publicly say Right. what we had, Right.\N如果我没有公开说明我们所拥有的情况，那么。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:52.52,1:14:56.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,everybody would be second-guessing, are they short-changed, are we being, you know,\N每个人都会怀疑，他们是否被亏待了，我们是不是。
Dialogue: 0,1:14:56.57,1:15:04.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,and so And so it was it was my way of of essentially handling um every single conversation where I'm disappointing people.\N所以，这实际上是我处理所有令人失望对话的一种方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:04.16,1:15:04.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:04.56,1:15:10.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and let's So pretty much every customer would buy more from you if you could deliver more to By far.\N嗯，基本上，如果你能提供更多，几乎所有客户都会向你购买更多。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:10.92,1:15:16.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then And then since then, of course, now we have new orders Right. almost almost weekly and daily.\N然后，从那以后，当然，我们现在几乎每周、每天都有新订单。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:16.94,1:15:22.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And so So um uh in addition, however, uh we're getting more supply.\N而且，不过，我们正获得更多的供应。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:22.50,1:15:26.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Some of the supply that that is limiting us is land power shell downstream.\N一些限制我们供应的瓶颈在于下游的土地、电力与厂房。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:26.56,1:15:29.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so a couple weeks ago we announced 2 GW in Australia.\N所以几周前，我们宣布了在澳大利亚的 2 吉瓦项目。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:29.72,1:15:30.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:30.12,1:15:31.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that's a very big deal.\N这是个非常重大的事情。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:31.71,1:15:33.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,2 GW to us is like $80 billion.\N对我们来说，2 吉瓦相当于 800 亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:33.32,1:15:33.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:33.72,1:15:34.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Huge.\N非常巨大。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:34.12,1:15:42.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And then And then um um I'm hoping when I go to Europe with UTC, you know, we'll be able to announce some some uh new partnerships there.\N然后，嗯，我希望当我带着 UTC 去欧洲时，我们能宣布一些新的合作。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:42.08,1:15:44.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And unlock more more land power shell.\N并且解锁更多的土地、电力与厂房。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:45.04,1:15:48.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So this is land power shell is is clearly one of the obstacles.\N所以，土地、电力与厂房显然就是其中一个障碍。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:48.93,1:15:53.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And this is this is a an an area where Nvidia has a a huge advantage.\N而且这正是英伟达拥有巨大优势的领域。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:53.40,1:15:53.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:15:53.68,1:16:02.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, because based on what we build, if if uh there's a a new cloud um uh and uh this new cloud like CoreWeave or Nebius,\N你知道，基于我们所构建的体系，如果出现一个新的云服务商，比如 CoreWeave 或 Nebius，
Dialogue: 0,1:16:02.62,1:16:10.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,um and they would like to to scale out their business, Nvidia has the entire full stack complete AI infrastructure.\N而且他们希望扩展业务，英伟达拥有完整的端到端 AI 基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:10.76,1:16:14.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So we could support them as they're scaling out.\N所以，当他们扩展业务时，我们可以提供支持。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:14.15,1:16:20.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so we We could build in places and we can build with partners and customers that nobody else can.\N而且我们可以在别人无法做到的地方进行建设，也可以与合作伙伴和客户共同推进。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:20.15,1:16:23.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh uh and and so I I think this this gives us a lot more resilience.\N所以我认为这让我们具备了更强的韧性。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:23.73,1:16:34.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,But none nonetheless, uh as we as we continue to increase supply upstream and downstream, uh you know, uh one of the critical areas is substrate.\N但无论如何，随着我们持续提升上下游的供应能力，一个关键领域仍然是基板。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:34.78,1:16:38.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Substrates are getting larger and there are more chips.\N基板正在变得越来越大，芯片数量也越来越多。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:38.52,1:16:41.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So it's working against them in two ways.\N所以这从两个方面对对手形成了压制。
Dialogue: 0,1:16:41.09,1:16:50.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single chip that's being shipped uses more of the material and so So these these organic materials are are are really hard to make\N每一块出货的芯片都在使用更多的材料，因此这些有机材料的制造非常困难
Dialogue: 0,1:16:50.53,1:17:01.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,at the precision that we need because the as the packages get larger the the the coefficient the thermal coefficients and the way we stack things\N在我们需要的精度下，由于封装尺寸增大，热膨胀系数以及我们堆叠方式的变化
Dialogue: 0,1:17:01.24,1:17:08.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,make it really hard to handle things like warpage and you know and various various manufacturing defects and and so at the scale that we\N使得处理翘曲等问题变得极为困难，而且各种制造缺陷也难以避免，因此在我们这样的规模下
Dialogue: 0,1:17:08.81,1:17:16.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,do we have to be very size and we need really great partners And so that's that's supply constraint and just those are just some examples.\N我们必须非常注重尺寸控制，并需要非常优秀的合作伙伴，因此这就是供应限制，这只是其中一些例子
Dialogue: 0,1:17:16.68,1:17:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Silicon photonics is is supply constrained and so So everything is supply constrained and so we're going to keep working on it.\N硅光子学也面临供应限制，因此所有领域都面临供应限制，所以我们将继续努力解决
Dialogue: 0,1:17:24.08,1:17:26.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have 18 months to do so and you know every single week that goes by\N我还有18个月时间来完成，而且每周过去，
Dialogue: 0,1:17:26.97,1:17:31.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,we increase but nonetheless every we keep increasing more supply and our order books keeps going up.\N供应量都在增加，我们的订单量也持续上升
Dialogue: 0,1:17:31.68,1:17:32.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错
Dialogue: 0,1:17:32.28,1:17:36.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it's going to be hard to close that gap for a few years.\N因此在未来几年内，缩小这一差距将非常困难
Dialogue: 0,1:17:36.20,1:17:38.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take a look at this chart.\N请看这张图表
Dialogue: 0,1:17:38.76,1:17:41.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know This is like a deposition.\N你知道，这就像一种沉积过程
Dialogue: 0,1:17:41.52,1:17:42.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,No it's not.\N不，不是的
Dialogue: 0,1:17:42.44,1:17:50.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Excuse me Mr. Usually it goes like this Mr. Huang Please please now Please now look at exhibit The deposition.\N打扰一下，先生。通常情况是这样的，黄先生，请，请现在，请现在看证据清单。证词。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:50.12,1:17:54.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay so the gray line this is was the consensus at the start of 2025.\N好的，这条灰线是2025年初的共识。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:54.91,1:17:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,This was the consensus for Nvidia at the start of 2025.\N这是2025年初对英伟达的共识。
Dialogue: 0,1:17:58.92,1:18:04.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,The blue line was Altimeter's forecast way back then so we were a lot higher than the consensus.\N这条蓝线是当时阿尔蒂米特的预测，所以我们当时比共识高出很多。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:04.60,1:18:10.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,The green line is now where the new consensus is based upon your guidance and so one of the things that\N这条绿线现在是基于你们的指引所形成的新的共识，其中有一件事让我震惊的是
Dialogue: 0,1:18:10.42,1:18:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,blows my mind about this is the 25 people who get paid to just forecast what this company is going to do.\N这里有25个人，他们的工作就是预测这家公司的表现。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:17.04,1:18:23.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Their consensus of all their ideas right was off by a couple hundred percent right just at the beginning\N他们所有人的共识，一开始就在几百个百分点上出现了偏差。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:23.71,1:18:28.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,of 20 uh Oh no This time last at this time last year not even 25 Is my line?\N2025年初，哦不，是去年这个时候，甚至不到25个人，是我的线吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:18:28.36,1:18:34.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes that was that was the consensus at this time last year okay one year ago.\N是的，这就是去年这个时候的共识，一年前。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:34.12,1:18:34.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:34.98,1:18:42.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So in a year the consensus forecast has shifted up by 100% to 200% for this company.\N一年之内，对这家公司的共识预测上调了100%到200%。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:42.40,1:18:42.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:42.92,1:18:43.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Extraordinary.\N非凡的。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:43.62,1:18:49.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like in in my 20 plus years of doing this, you don't often see consensus being off by that much.\N就像我二十多年从事这项工作以来，很少见到共识偏差这么大。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:49.37,1:18:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And yet the stock's only up 20%.\N但股价仅上涨了20%。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:52.56,1:18:59.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, you literally doubled what the revenue forecast was and the free cash flow forecast was for the company.\N你实际上将公司的营收预测和自由现金流预测都翻了一倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:18:59.08,1:19:04.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're now trading at 13 to 14 times earnings depending upon who you're looking at.\N你现在市盈率在13到14倍之间，具体取决于你参考的数据来源。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:05.03,1:19:12.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, what do you think the market is saying about Nvidia or about the confidence in the expectations of the market, right?\N那么，你认为市场在暗示什么？关于英伟达，或者关于市场预期的信心，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:19:12.36,1:19:14.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,To cause that to be the case.\N导致这种情况发生。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:14.24,1:19:18.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because usually if you see it shift up by that much, the stock would have shifted up by a lot more.\N因为通常如果预期大幅上调，股价也会大幅上涨。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:18.84,1:19:25.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh first of all, the the for a company to be as large as us gaining share tells you something about the resilience Yes.\N首先，一家像我们这样规模的公司还能持续获得市场份额，这说明了某种韧性，是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:25.56,1:19:29.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and the the the size and scale of our advantage.\N以及我们优势的规模和体量。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:30.00,1:19:30.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:30.60,1:19:33.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so Is that advantage increasing or decreasing?\N那么，这种优势是在扩大还是在缩小？
Dialogue: 0,1:19:33.61,1:19:35.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is your moat increasing or decreasing?\N你的护城河是在扩大还是在缩小？
Dialogue: 0,1:19:35.08,1:19:35.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Increasing.\N在扩大。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:35.84,1:19:36.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Increasing.\N在扩大。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:36.80,1:19:37.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Increasing.\N在扩大。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:36.84,1:19:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Your competitive moat is increasing at scale.\N你的竞争优势护城河正在规模化扩大。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:40.08,1:19:40.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, let me give you an example.\N是的，我来举个例子。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:40.79,1:19:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's just do a thought experiment right now.\N我们现在就做个思想实验。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:43.00,1:19:49.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you had to hand somebody a hundred billion dollar check to place a purchase order right now for a next generation.\N如果你必须当场交给某人一张百亿美元的支票，才能立刻下单采购下一代产品。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:49.96,1:19:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:50.68,1:19:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you if you want to get in line um for Vera Rubin Ultra it's close to placing order time.\N如果你想排队预订 Vera Rubin Ultra，现在几乎就是下单时刻了。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:57.32,1:19:58.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N太厉害了。
Dialogue: 0,1:19:59.00,1:20:00.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sight unseen.\N未见实物就下单。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:00.12,1:20:00.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:00.96,1:20:01.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:20:01.36,1:20:02.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,But they have the confidence.\N但他们有自信。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:02.56,1:20:06.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, let's say there's a you got to place a hundred billion dollars on somebody.\N所以，假设你要把一百亿美元押在某个人身上。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:06.63,1:20:07.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,One.\N一个。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:07.20,1:20:09.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh how do you know it's going to be any good?\N你怎么知道它会有多好？
Dialogue: 0,1:20:09.16,1:20:09.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:09.44,1:20:12.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,But because Nvidia builds it, you know it's going to be better than Vera Rubin.\N但因为是英伟达打造的，你知道它会比维拉·鲁宾更出色。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:12.28,1:20:12.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:12.64,1:20:13.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Vera Rubin's awesome.\N而且维拉·鲁宾真的很棒。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:13.68,1:20:14.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:14.12,1:20:19.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason why Vera Rubin you the reason why everybody had confidence in Vera Rubin is because Grace Hopper was awesome.\N维拉·鲁宾之所以让大家有信心，是因为格蕾丝·霍珀太厉害了。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:19.20,1:20:20.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:20.08,1:20:26.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so and the world of computing the the workloads that these computers do are so complex.\N在计算领域，这些计算机所处理的工作负载非常复杂。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:26.17,1:20:29.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't just have like measure one benchmark.\N你不能只看一个基准测试的结果。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:29.44,1:20:29.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:29.82,1:20:30.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:30.20,1:20:31.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, it's fifty billion dollars.\N你知道，这可是五百亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:31.96,1:20:32.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:32.80,1:20:38.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the number of technologies that have to come together to deliver the performance is insane, you know?\N要实现这种性能，需要汇聚如此多的技术，简直难以置信，你知道吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:20:38.56,1:20:46.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So So, the question is sight unseen, who can you place a 50 100 billion dollar order on?\N所以，不看具体细节的情况下，你能把五百亿到一千亿美元的订单交给谁？
Dialogue: 0,1:20:46.36,1:20:47.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:47.24,1:20:48.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're literally the only one.\N我们确实是唯一一个。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:48.92,1:20:50.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:50.08,1:20:54.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, back when it was place a PO a billion dollar PO, that was challenging enough.\N现在，回想当初下一份十亿美元的采购订单时，就已经足够有挑战性了。
Dialogue: 0,1:20:54.64,1:21:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if you had place a 100 million dollar PO, and the the the the system is sitting right in front of you.\N但如果你要下一份一亿美元的采购订单，而系统就摆在你面前。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:00.48,1:21:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could just bench you can benchmark the chips.\N你完全可以对芯片进行基准测试。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:03.36,1:21:03.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:03.88,1:21:04.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:21:04.19,1:21:06.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you benchmark these systems?\N你该如何对这些系统进行基准测试？
Dialogue: 0,1:21:06.60,1:21:08.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just building it is a miracle.\N只是把它们造出来，就已经是个奇迹了。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:08.48,1:21:09.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:09.52,1:21:13.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, so if somebody wants to do an evaluation, I'm happy to support it,\N你知道，如果有人想做评估，我很乐意支持，
Dialogue: 0,1:21:13.50,1:21:19.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,but you're going to need to give me a giant data center, and we're going to need a couple of years to retrofit it, and you know?\N但你得给我一个大型数据中心，我们还得花两三年时间去改造它，你明白吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:21:19.60,1:21:21.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you can't even benchmark these things anymore.\N所以，现在你甚至都无法对这些系统进行基准测试了。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:22.04,1:21:22.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:22.84,1:21:23.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Interesting.\N有趣。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:23.60,1:21:26.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, it's exactly what happened with TSMC.\N所以，这正是台积电发生的情况。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:26.40,1:21:26.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:26.84,1:21:32.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,The reason why we give 100% of our business to TSMC is because they're the only company in the world that I can plan 5 years out.\N我们把全部业务都交给台积电的原因是，它们是全球唯一一家我能提前五年规划的公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:32.72,1:21:33.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:33.08,1:21:39.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And know it's And sight unseen, know that that transistor is going to be really good because it's better than that one, better than that one.\N而且，即使没有亲眼见过，我也能确信那颗晶体管会非常出色，因为它比之前的更好，比之前的更好。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:39.28,1:21:40.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:40.64,1:21:44.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that they will have capacity for me, and that they know how to work with my business team,\N而且他们能为我提供产能，也清楚如何与我的业务团队协作，
Dialogue: 0,1:21:44.32,1:21:48.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,that they have the agility to handle all of my ups and downs, and you know,\N他们具备应对我所有起伏的灵活性，你也知道，
Dialogue: 0,1:21:48.61,1:21:53.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,for example, to deal with with the fact that I went from gray to blue to green.\N比如说，应对我从灰色到蓝色再到绿色的转变。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:53.48,1:21:53.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:21:54.04,1:21:54.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:54.60,1:21:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have to be big enough to go for help me go from gray to blue to green.\N它们必须足够大，才能帮助我从灰色过渡到蓝色，再过渡到绿色。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:57.68,1:21:58.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,1:21:58.44,1:22:00.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And there's no other company in the world that could help me do that.\N世界上没有其他公司能帮我实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:01.04,1:22:01.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:01.52,1:22:10.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And to have and and have all these different process technologies from silicon photonics to logic to memory to it push pull push pull packaging.\N而且我们拥有从硅光子学到逻辑、内存，再到封装的各类不同工艺技术，实现推拉式、循环式的发展。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:10.84,1:22:14.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, the number of things that we do is so dynamic.\N我们所做的事情数量之多，动态性之强，令人难以想象。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:14.56,1:22:14.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:14.88,1:22:19.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, how do you possibly do that with a company that is 1/10 their size?\N那么，你怎么可能用一家规模只有他们十分之一的公司做到这一点呢？
Dialogue: 0,1:22:19.49,1:22:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's impossible.\N这是不可能的。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:21.16,1:22:24.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I think the big idea is this.\N所以，我认为核心理念是这样的。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:24.12,1:22:30.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because we're building infrastructure for the planet, and Nvidia has become an infrastructure company.\N因为我们正在为整个星球构建基础设施，而英伟达已经成长为一家基础设施公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:30.32,1:22:31.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:31.16,1:22:36.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And because these infrastructures cost so much money and they're moving and technology is moving so fast.\N而且这些基础设施成本极高，技术又在飞速发展。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:36.16,1:22:37.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:37.12,1:22:45.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're practically, you know, the combination of the trust the the fact that we run everything You know,\N我们实际上，你知道，是信任的结合，因为我们运行着所有东西，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,1:22:45.39,1:22:53.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,so it started out with some some GPT models, um but look at the flash attention mechanisms that were were were invented.\N所以最初我们用了一些 GPT 模型，但看看那些被发明出来的闪存注意力机制。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:53.52,1:22:59.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,The way that we paralyze the models and shard across NVLink 72 and how all of that changed.\N我们如何并行化模型并在 NVLink 72 上分片，以及所有这些变化。
Dialogue: 0,1:22:59.35,1:23:04.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,MOE changed and now people are talking about transformer diffusion models that are hybrid,\NMOE 发生了改变，现在人们开始谈论混合的 Transformer 扩散模型，
Dialogue: 0,1:23:04.65,1:23:09.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,SSMs that are transformers hybrids, and all these different technologies are all, right?\N以及混合了 Transformer 的 SSM，所有这些不同的技术都汇聚在一起，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:23:09.36,1:23:10.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,The evolution of all that.\N所有这些的演进过程。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:10.76,1:23:12.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We know that it all runs on CUDA.\N我们知道这一切都运行在 CUDA 上。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:12.60,1:23:13.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:13.36,1:23:19.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is the only We We don't know whether you need to do more pre-training, post-training, or just agentic inference.\N这是唯一的，我们不知道你是否需要做更多的预训练、后训练，还是仅仅代理式推理。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:19.38,1:23:21.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, turns out we run it all anyways.\N但结果是，我们无论如何都运行所有这些。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:21.56,1:23:21.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:21.84,1:23:28.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you could build a $50 billion data center and know that the fungibility of the work and if something were to happen,\N所以你可以建设一个价值500亿美元的数据中心，并且知道工作负载的可互换性，以及万一发生什么情况时，
Dialogue: 0,1:23:29.04,1:23:35.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,you you know, for whatever reason unknown, you wanted to, if you will, sublease half of your capacity to somebody.\N无论出于什么原因，你想要，如果你愿意的话，将你一半的容量转租给他人。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:35.56,1:23:36.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nvidia's completely fungible.\N英伟达的设备完全具备可互换性。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:36.92,1:23:37.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:37.40,1:23:42.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're fungible in workload, we're fungible in models, we're fungible across customers.\N我们在工作负载上可互换，模型上可互换，跨客户之间也可互换。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:42.56,1:23:44.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're deployable everywhere in the world.\N我们可以部署到全球任何地方。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:44.30,1:23:48.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,You start a company in Europe, you start a company in United States, but guess what?\N你在欧洲创办一家公司，在美国创办一家公司，但你猜怎么着？
Dialogue: 0,1:23:48.50,1:23:51.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,You would like your customer, you want to serve customers in Europe, you want to serve customers in Japan.\N你希望你的客户，你想服务欧洲的客户，也想服务日本的客户。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:52.03,1:23:53.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, turns out we're already there.\N结果发现，我们已经在那儿了。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:53.77,1:23:56.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nvidia's Nvidia's infrastructure is already there.\N英伟达的基础设施已经遍布全球。
Dialogue: 0,1:23:56.71,1:24:00.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,So OpenAI wants to go to Europe, we'll take them there in a heartbeat.\N所以如果OpenAI想进军欧洲，我们能立刻带他们过去。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:00.85,1:24:02.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,If they want to go to India, in a heartbeat.\N如果他们想去印度，那简直毫不犹豫。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:02.63,1:24:03.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,If they want Isn't that right?\N如果他们想去，不是吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:24:03.82,1:24:06.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,If Anthropic wants to go to Japan, Korea, in a heartbeat.\N如果 Anthropic 想去日本或韩国，那也是一样毫不犹豫。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:06.31,1:24:07.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're already there.\N我们已经在那儿了。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:07.48,1:24:07.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:07.88,1:24:09.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these architectures are already there.\N所有这些架构都已经在那儿了。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:09.96,1:24:18.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I think the the if you take Nvidia in the whole and then you come back and you say, "Okay, I want to do the thought experiment.\N所以我认为，如果你把英伟达整体考虑进去，然后再回过头来设想一下：“好，我想做个思想实验。”
Dialogue: 0,1:24:18.85,1:24:22.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to place a $100 billion dollars Right.\N我想投入 1000 亿美元，怎么样？
Dialogue: 0,1:24:22.60,1:24:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you do it?\N你该怎么做？
Dialogue: 0,1:24:24.16,1:24:31.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,A year ago we were sitting here and the consensus forecast was that you were going to be flat or shrink in 2027.\N一年前我们坐在这里时，共识预测是你们在 2027 年将持平或萎缩。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:31.64,1:24:35.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now the consensus forecast is you're going to grow 74% okay?\N现在共识预测是你们将增长 74%，好吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:24:35.59,1:24:42.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you know I I just want to let people let that sit in because a lot of people follow these consensus forecasts right?\N所以我想让大家好好想想这一点，因为很多人会关注这些共识预测，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.07,1:24:44.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it was really wrong okay?\N而且这确实错了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:24:44.20,1:24:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,It it they were forecasting go back and listen to your podcast from last time?\N他们当时在预测，回头去听听你们上次的播客吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:24:49.72,1:24:50.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right you told them.\N没错，你当时就告诉过他们了。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:50.44,1:24:55.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah yeah I explained Listen ladies and gentlemen I did explain everything.\N对，对，我解释过了，女士们先生们，我真的把一切都解释清楚了。
Dialogue: 0,1:24:55.52,1:25:01.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I look I look at a 2029 There was a there was wasn't it an ROI question?\N所以我看看2029年，当时不是有个投资回报率的问题吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:25:01.36,1:25:01.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:01.92,1:25:07.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then there was there was this custom yeah custom versus general purpose.\N然后还有这个定制化和通用型的对比。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:07.96,1:25:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,The reason why Nvidia's general purpose is so I can have all this fungibility.\N英伟达的通用性之所以如此重要，是因为我能获得这种可互换性。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:11.44,1:25:12.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:12.12,1:25:14.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the benefit of fungibility is low risk.\N可互换性的优势在于风险低。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:14.76,1:25:15.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:15.72,1:25:20.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And low risk really comes in to play when you're placing big dollars.\N而当你要投入大量资金时，低风险就真正凸显出来了。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:20.60,1:25:24.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you're building out 50 100 billion dollars worth of infrastructure you need to know\N当你正在建设价值500亿到1000亿美元的基础设施时，你必须清楚
Dialogue: 0,1:25:24.59,1:25:30.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,that that infrastructure is going to be really good for a long time no matter what.\N这些基础设施无论发生什么情况，都能长期保持卓越性能。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:30.50,1:25:35.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So specialization is the enemy of fungibility.\N因此，专业化是可替代性的敌人。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:35.12,1:25:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Specialization is the enemy of durability.\N专业化是耐用性的敌人。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:39.60,1:25:48.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so long as I can prove that our performance is extraordinary and we prove that every single day.\N只要我能证明我们的性能确实非凡，并且每天都能证明这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:48.48,1:25:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,The moment we can prove that then fungibility and durability translates to rentability which translates to productivity.\N一旦我们能证明这一点，可替代性和耐用性就会转化为可租赁性，进而转化为生产力。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:56.20,1:25:57.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And financeability.\N以及可融资性。
Dialogue: 0,1:25:57.36,1:26:01.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And fi- and therefore financeability which leads to the lowest TCO.\N以及因此带来的可融资性，最终带来最低的总拥有成本。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:01.40,1:26:02.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right right exactly.\N对，完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:02.84,1:26:03.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:03.72,1:26:07.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well now now you're buying back the largest amount in history.\N现在你正在回购历史上最大规模的股份。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:07.06,1:26:13.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know on my math you know you could probably buy upwards of 10% of the company back within the next two years.\N按我的计算，你可能在接下来两年内回购公司10%以上的股份。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:13.92,1:26:17.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,At Goldman you called Nvidia you know the first growth value company.\N在高盛时，你曾称英伟达为你知道的第一个成长型价值公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:18.04,1:26:20.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:20.60,1:26:24.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sounds a lot like uh Apple's pitch to Oh, is that right?\N听起来很像苹果当初的宣传，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:26:24.33,1:26:24.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:24.64,1:26:25.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is that right?\N是这样吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:26:25.40,1:26:28.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, or or more Yeah, more that they that they could return the capital.\N对，或者更准确地说，是他们能够回报资本。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:28.40,1:26:28.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It worked.\N这招奏效了。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:29.04,1:26:29.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, for sure.\N对，毫无疑问。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:29.80,1:26:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It worked.\N这招奏效了。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:30.28,1:26:33.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Went from 300 at the time $30 to 300.\N从当时的300美元涨到了3000美元。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:33.64,1:26:34.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:34.04,1:26:34.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,300 plus.\N3000以上。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:34.60,1:26:38.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in a lot of ways we're going through a similar transition.\N从很多方面来看，我们正经历着类似的转型。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:38.33,1:26:45.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,For ex- For example, the the thing I did I forgot to mention is and and and Brad, I think you were about to ask me about that.\N比如说，我之前忘了提一件事，布拉德，我想你正要问我这个。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:45.97,1:26:56.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know, most of our investment and financing um uh partnership strategies is trying to teach trying to set up uh two business models.\N你知道，我们大部分的投资和融资，以及合作策略，都是在尝试教授和建立两种商业模式。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:56.60,1:26:57.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:57.04,1:26:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Two new business models.\N两种全新的商业模式。
Dialogue: 0,1:26:58.92,1:27:07.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um uh one business model we've been working on for some time and it will be accelerated uh in the near future is software licensing.\N我们已经持续一段时间在推进其中一种商业模式，它将在不久的将来加速发展，那就是软件授权。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:07.08,1:27:07.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:07.52,1:27:10.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, the body of software that we have in our companies is extraordinary.\N我们公司所拥有的软件体系非常庞大。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:10.88,1:27:14.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that data center is so large, imagine all the software that runs in it.\N那个数据中心如此巨大，可以想象其中运行着多少软件。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:14.40,1:27:16.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we provide the entire stack.\N我们提供完整的软件栈。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:16.84,1:27:20.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, and our entire stack is completely industrial strength.\N而且我们的整个软件栈都是完全工业级的。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:20.59,1:27:23.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,For the CSPs, they want to run their own stack.\N对于云服务商来说，他们希望运行自己的软件栈。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:23.20,1:27:23.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:23.56,1:27:27.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we license or we give them our software open source and then they take\N所以我们把软件开源授权给他们，然后他们拿去
Dialogue: 0,1:27:27.24,1:27:31.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,it and they modify it and they integrate into theirs and then they operate their services.\N修改并集成到自己的系统中，再运营他们的服务。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:31.72,1:27:36.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,But for a lot of the world's companies, they don't have the IT department, they don't have the software department to do it.\N但对世界上很多公司来说，他们没有IT部门，也没有软件部门来完成这项工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:36.69,1:27:38.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So they need me to maintain it.\N所以他们需要我来维护。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.28,1:27:38.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.44,1:27:47.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so because AI in the last several year was largely focused on re- uh on training, but now they're moving into deployment.\N因为过去几年AI主要集中在训练上，但现在他们正转向部署。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:47.52,1:27:48.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:48.08,1:27:53.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,They need to operate these as factories and they need to they need to know that I'm on the hook.\N他们需要把AI当作工厂来运营，而且必须知道我负有责任。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:53.32,1:27:59.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm on the SLA to support it and maintain it, keep it secure, keep it safe Right. for as long as we shall live.\N我对服务的SLA负责，要持续支持、维护、确保安全和稳定，直到我们生命终结。
Dialogue: 0,1:27:59.68,1:28:03.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so software license for our enterprise business will be very, very large.\N因此，我们企业业务的软件授权将非常庞大。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:03.40,1:28:03.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:03.96,1:28:07.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you know, if we if if our software license is, you know, just roughly say,\N所以你知道，如果我们的软件许可，比如说，大致是每块GPU每年几千美元，用于简单的数学计算，
Dialogue: 0,1:28:07.88,1:28:13.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,for for for for simple math, a couple of thousand dollars per GPU per year, and we have millions of GPUs.\N而我们拥有数百万块GPU，
Dialogue: 0,1:28:13.68,1:28:14.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对的。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:14.16,1:28:19.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have we just we ship, you know, 20 million GPUs say a year, I'm growing.\N我们每年大概出货2000万块GPU，而且还在增长。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:19.36,1:28:23.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, half of it goes into world's enterprise, it adds up.\N所以其中一半进入了全球企业市场，加起来数额巨大。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:23.12,1:28:23.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:28:23.41,1:28:28.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so I'm fairly certain this is going to be a very big part of our business, software license.\N因此我相当确定，软件许可将会成为我们业务中非常重要的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:28.20,1:28:35.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, of course, there there some some clouds that that uh rely on Nvidia for our full stack.\N当然，也有一些云服务商完全依赖英伟达的完整技术栈。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:35.48,1:28:35.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:36.00,1:28:39.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,They rely on us for our off-take, our ecosystem.\N他们依赖我们提供产品采购和生态系统支持。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:39.72,1:28:40.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:39.88,1:28:47.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,They also rely on us for maybe as an investment partner in helping them secure secure their financing and capital.\N他们还可能依赖我们作为投资伙伴，帮助他们获得融资和资本支持。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:47.16,1:28:48.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:48.24,1:28:50.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,They've secured land power shell, they're regional champion,\N他们已获得土地、电力与厂房，是区域冠军，
Dialogue: 0,1:28:50.74,1:28:55.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,they got all kinds of stuff working in their in their advantage, but these three areas they need our support on.\N他们拥有各种有利条件，但在这三个领域，他们需要我们的支持。
Dialogue: 0,1:28:55.69,1:29:00.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, in in those kind of relationships, it's very likely that we'll move to rev share.\N因此，在这类合作关系中，我们很可能会采用收益分成模式。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:00.27,1:29:05.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we'll make an investment, we'll get the benefit of the sale up front, but we'll also have the benefit of rev share going forward.\N我们将进行投资， upfront 获得销售收益，同时未来也能持续获得收益分成。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:05.98,1:29:09.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you know, we're we're not a cloud service provider,\N所以，我们并不是云服务提供商，
Dialogue: 0,1:29:09.44,1:29:16.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,um but we're going to be providing off-take and providing software support for them for for, you know, 4 5 10 years.\N但我们将在未来四到五年内为他们提供产品采购支持和软件支持。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:16.16,1:29:19.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we ought to get some economic return on that.\N因此，我们理应获得相应的经济回报。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:19.66,1:29:21.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, rev share is going to be significant.\N所以，收益分成将非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:21.92,1:29:23.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like a store sale.\N就像一次商店销售。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:23.12,1:29:27.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,I just described two new growth vectors independent of the hardware sale of our company,\N我刚刚描述了两个与公司硬件销售无关的新增长方向，
Dialogue: 0,1:29:27.87,1:29:32.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,and it's much more related to the installed base of our platform.\N它们更与我们平台的现有部署规模密切相关。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:32.60,1:29:36.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's the benefit of software licensing if you have no installed base?\N如果没有已安装用户基础，软件授权有什么好处？
Dialogue: 0,1:29:36.37,1:29:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and how could you have rev share if there's no off-take?\N嗯，如果没有任何采购方，你又如何实现收益分成？
Dialogue: 0,1:29:39.20,1:29:39.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:39.56,1:29:39.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:29:39.91,1:29:44.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, that the installed base element, the richness of our software stack, the off-take,\N所以，已安装用户基础、我们软件栈的丰富程度，以及采购方的规模，
Dialogue: 0,1:29:44.87,1:29:48.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,the richness of our off-take and the ecosystem that we have around the world,\N以及我们全球范围内构建的生态系统，
Dialogue: 0,1:29:48.47,1:29:54.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's going to fuel the the Uh well, one of the one of the ways, you know, so we're talking about this trading at 13 times.\N这将推动……嗯，其中一个方式，你知道，我们正在讨论的是市盈率13倍。
Dialogue: 0,1:29:54.47,1:29:56.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, when Ten and Luca went to see Warren Buffett,\N你知道，当十和卢卡去见沃伦·巴菲特时，
Dialogue: 0,1:29:56.84,1:30:02.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,and one of the reasons that Buffett has said he doesn't like technology companies is they they have this hit,\N巴菲特曾表示他不喜欢科技公司，因为这些公司往往有这种现象，
Dialogue: 0,1:30:02.38,1:30:04.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,they produce an enormous amount of free cash flow,\N他们产生巨额的自由现金流，
Dialogue: 0,1:30:04.97,1:30:09.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,and rather than ever giving any of it back to the shareholders, they go and spend it on something else.\N却从未将其中任何一部分返还给股东，而是拿去投资其他项目。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:09.87,1:30:15.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And oftentimes the something else isn't as good as the thing that caused them to generate the cash flow in the first place.\N而这些其他项目，往往不如最初带来现金流的业务那么出色。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:15.15,1:30:22.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,You guys are now spending over 50% of your free cash flow buying back your stock effectively returning it you know,\N你们现在正将超过50%的自由现金流用于股票回购，实际上相当于把钱还给了股东。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:22.23,1:30:25.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,to shareholders while you have this exponential growth at the same time.\N同时拥有这种指数级增长时，向股东们汇报。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:25.34,1:30:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,As we've already discussed We said 50.\N正如我们之前讨论过的，我们提到过50。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:28.16,1:30:28.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:28.64,1:30:30.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think this last quarter we did 60 some odd.\N我认为上个季度我们做到了六十几。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:30.60,1:30:31.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Correct.\N正确。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:31.16,1:30:36.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we're we're we're going to increase You know, we invest in really high-quality companies as you guys know.\N是的，我们会增加投资，正如你们所知，我们专注于投资高质量的公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:37.04,1:30:46.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and and you know, the last couple of years, whoever Nvidia buys from, whoever Jensen's buys from, you got to invest in that company.\N而且你知道，过去几年里，无论英伟达买谁的，无论黄仁勋买谁的，你都得投资那家公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:46.32,1:30:50.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now the new the new word on the street is whoever Jensen invests in, you got to invest in that company.\N现在街头最新的消息是，黄仁勋投资了哪家公司，你就要跟着投资那家公司。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:50.46,1:30:51.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it and and it's true.\N而且确实如此。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:51.58,1:30:55.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because you know, like you, we're we're in we're in the ecosystem.\N原因在于，就像你一样，我们也在这个生态系统里。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:55.96,1:30:58.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're in the we're in the flow of information.\N我们正处在信息的流动之中。
Dialogue: 0,1:30:58.31,1:31:00.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We know who's doing what. investments together.\N我们清楚谁在做什么，以及共同投资的情况。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:00.84,1:31:02.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and we know a lot of smart people.\N是的，而且我们认识很多聪明人。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:02.52,1:31:02.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:02.76,1:31:06.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we want to back these people when they when they you know, want to do something great.\N我们希望在他们想要做大事时，能够支持他们。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:06.84,1:31:09.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so we're kind of in on the inside.\N所以我们实际上处于内部位置。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:09.10,1:31:13.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we we have a lot of information and so our investments are you know, well informed.\N我们掌握大量信息，因此我们的投资决策是充分知情的。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:13.76,1:31:14.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:14.04,1:31:14.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:14.32,1:31:18.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And not to mention Nvidia's also in the ecosystem and so we can help them succeed.\N更不用说英伟达也在这个生态系统中，我们可以帮助他们取得成功。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:18.84,1:31:19.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:19.32,1:31:22.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so there's a lot of different reasons why the investments turn out great.\N因此，投资表现优异的原因有很多。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:22.36,1:31:30.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but as a percentage of of our total um uh cash generation, it's going to decline very rapidly.\N嗯，但就我们总现金生成量的比例而言，这个比例将迅速下降。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:30.68,1:31:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Partly because OpenAI and Anthropic isn't going to come a That's right.\N部分原因在于，OpenAI 和 Anthropic 不会再来。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:34.88,1:31:36.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,opportunity is not going to come around again.\N这个机会不会再出现了。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:36.86,1:31:43.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Frankly and and then secondarily um our our cash flow generation is is growing quite fast.\N坦率地说，其次我们的现金流生成正在快速增长。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:43.40,1:31:43.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:43.84,1:31:44.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:44.08,1:31:51.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and and to that point, it seems to me that if you're buying back that much and the durability of the revenues,\N说到这一点，我觉得如果你回购这么多，而且收入的持久性，
Dialogue: 0,1:31:51.64,1:31:55.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think as you've described here today, is longer than people expect.\N我认为正如你今天所描述的，比人们预期的要长。
Dialogue: 0,1:31:55.82,1:32:03.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think that's the one place people are still hanging too much on this is only going to last as long As I asked you this on the pod the other day,\N我觉得人们仍然过于担心，以为这只能持续到我前几天在播客里问你的那个问题，
Dialogue: 0,1:32:03.60,1:32:04.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,how long until the bubble burst?\N什么时候泡沫会破裂？
Dialogue: 0,1:32:04.99,1:32:09.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think you said something about two to three years you have good visibility that, you know,\N你提到可能是两到三年，你有很好的可见性，知道需求确实存在，至于那之后会怎样，谁说得准呢。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:09.88,1:32:15.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,the demand is there and who knows kind of after that and I heard some people saying, "Oh, it may only be two years before this burst."\N我听到有些人说：“哦，可能两年内就会破裂。”
Dialogue: 0,1:32:15.84,1:32:23.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,But when I look at this, like this is fundamentally a re-architecture of all global compute forever.\N但当我看这个时，这本质上是全球计算架构的永久性重构。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:23.48,1:32:23.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Forever.\N永远如此。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:23.86,1:32:26.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, unless there's a global depression, Yeah. right?\N所以，除非发生全球性经济衰退，否则是的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:32:26.64,1:32:32.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then every single year people are going to have to consume an enormous amount of Nvidia compute.\N那么，每年人们都将需要消耗大量英伟达的计算资源。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:32.20,1:32:39.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,so so the the way to think about that is is we were running in the um you know, the CSPs were running about half a trillion.\N所以，可以这样理解：我们过去在运行，云计算服务商（CSP）的规模大约是五千亿。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:39.31,1:32:46.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,The whole comp the whole industry, the whole world is running call it a trillion dollars of IT Right. build out each year.\N整个行业、整个世界每年都在投入约一万亿的IT支出，用于基础设施建设。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:46.71,1:32:47.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay?\N好的？
Dialogue: 0,1:32:47.30,1:32:52.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And every and every year more gets built and every five years or so some gets, you know,\N每年都会新建更多，每隔大约五年，就会有一些被折旧、关闭或下线。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:53.04,1:32:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,depreciated or turned off and and taken offline and so on and so forth and some of them some of it lasts longer.\N有些会折旧、关停、下线，等等，有些则能用得更久。
Dialogue: 0,1:32:58.92,1:33:07.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so so that that old world was in the retrieval way of doing com- computation and the new way of doing computation, you know,\N旧的世界是基于检索的计算方式，而新的计算方式则是……
Dialogue: 0,1:33:07.95,1:33:12.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,I've I've predicted that going out of the out of the decade so so three, four, let's say four,\N我预测，这种转变将在本十年末完成，比如三到四年，或者说是四到五年。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:12.89,1:33:18.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,let's say five and um I and my sense is that we're going to continue to grow from there.\N我的感觉是，从那时起，我们仍将持续增长。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:18.87,1:33:26.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you told me that the annual the annual capacity building, infrastructure building, refreshing,\N如果你说每年的算力建设、基础设施投入和更新……
Dialogue: 0,1:33:27.00,1:33:34.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,combination of new and old um uh refreshes runs around $10 trillion, I'm not even a little bit surprised.\N新旧结合的模式，其规模约为10万亿美元，我一点也不感到惊讶。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:34.56,1:33:34.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:34.88,1:33:35.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:35.56,1:33:38.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean just just again for people listening, you know,\N我的意思是，再强调一遍，对正在听的各位来说，你们知道，
Dialogue: 0,1:33:38.73,1:33:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,you think $4 trillion of annual spend by the end of the decade because every time you consume tokens,\N到本十年末，每年支出将达到4万亿美元，因为每次你使用词元，
Dialogue: 0,1:33:44.16,1:33:46.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,every time you use intelligence, you have to run the machine.\N每次你调用智能，都必须运行机器。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:46.94,1:33:48.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,The factory has to to run.\N工厂必须持续运转。
Dialogue: 0,1:33:48.91,1:33:54.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think you you've described that that's about 50%, you know, if you assume that,\N我认为你描述的约50%是合理的，如果你假设，
Dialogue: 0,1:33:54.12,1:34:00.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, $50 trillion dollars global GDP is you know, is related to knowledge work.\N全球GDP约50万亿美元与知识工作相关。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:00.11,1:34:08.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,If we get a 20% productivity gain over 5 years on that, like you've seen inside Nvidia, you've seen much bigger productivity gains inside Nvidia,\N如果我们在五年内实现20%的生产率提升，就像你在英伟达内部看到的那样，\N你甚至在英伟达内部看到了更大的生产率提升，
Dialogue: 0,1:34:08.78,1:34:14.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,but if you see that sort of productivity gain, then if we get 10 trillion dollars of incremental economic activity.\N但如果实现这种生产率提升，那么我们将迎来10万亿美元的增量经济活动。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:14.84,1:34:15.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, right.\N是的，没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:15.32,1:34:15.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:34:15.90,1:34:19.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,By the by by 2029, 2030, like that seems very reasonable.\N到2029年、2030年左右，这个时间点看起来非常合理。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:19.52,1:34:25.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you're just saying we'll spend half of that on capex on the intelligence, you know, to to produce it.\N而你只是说，我们会在智能的资本开支上花掉一半，也就是用来生产它。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:25.91,1:34:30.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so maybe you know, that's a good place for us to take a bit of an off-ramp.\N嗯，所以也许我们正好可以在这里稍微放缓一下。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:30.46,1:34:32.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've been incredibly generous.\N你真是太慷慨了。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:32.60,1:34:34.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I could go on forever.\N嗯，我还能说个没完。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:35.00,1:34:37.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I kind of want to wrap where we started.\N但我想回到我们一开始讨论的地方。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:37.30,1:34:37.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:34:38.04,1:34:45.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we look back Um if this was one of those eating, drinking podcasts A mukbang.\N如果我们回头看看，这就像是一档吃播或喝播类的播客。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:45.20,1:34:45.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could keep going.\N我们可以一直聊下去。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:45.97,1:34:48.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could keep going.\N我们可以一直聊下去。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:48.16,1:34:55.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it wasn't so long ago that the human condition was described as nasty, brutish, and short.\N去年还不到多久，人类的生存状态还被描述为肮脏、野蛮且短暂。
Dialogue: 0,1:34:55.40,1:34:55.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:34:56.00,1:35:04.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Was that last week or Innovation has really driven all human progress, mostly in the last 200 years.\N是上周还是说，创新确实推动了人类所有进步，尤其是过去200年。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:04.28,1:35:12.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um more time with family uh longer lives less time doing drudgery that humans\N更多陪伴家人的时间，更长的寿命，更少从事人类原本就不愿做的繁重劳作。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:12.44,1:35:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,really didn't want to do safer first generation where 63 years old is considered young.\N更安全的首代产品，63岁都算年轻。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:18.64,1:35:19.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:19.44,1:35:21.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly. still got, you know Exactly.\N没错，你懂的，就是这么回事。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:21.92,1:35:22.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,People call me young man.\N别人总叫我小伙子。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:22.96,1:35:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You safer, better lives.\N你们会拥有更安全、更美好的生活。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:27.52,1:35:31.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of this despite all of these concerns that you and I hear out there.\N尽管有你我听到的这些担忧。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:31.52,1:35:36.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And by the way, those same concerns were expressed at the beginning of the Industrial Revolution.\N顺便说一句，这些担忧在工业革命初期也曾被提出过。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:36.40,1:35:36.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:36.84,1:35:37.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:35:37.42,1:35:46.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's your level of confidence that in 5 years from now we will have made the right decisions and the world will be that much better place, right?\N五年后我们是否做出了正确的决策，世界因此变得更好，对此你有多大信心呢？
Dialogue: 0,1:35:46.76,1:35:50.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,That we describe because of the investment and all that we're doing.\N正是因为我们投入了大量资源，做了这么多事。
Dialogue: 0,1:35:50.99,1:35:55.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you more confident as we sit here today than you were 12 months ago?\N今天坐在这里，你比一年前更有信心吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:35:55.88,1:36:03.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm 99.99% just in in in in in service and honor of of a good friend not using zero and 100.\N我有99.99%的信心，纯粹是出于对一位好朋友的敬意，才没用0和100。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:03.76,1:36:15.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I'm 99.99% 99% confident that that um uh too many of us care do deeply that the outcome turns out well.\N嗯，我有99.99%的信心，因为太多人真心关心，希望结果能变好。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:15.52,1:36:15.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:16.04,1:36:24.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,That we will dedicate our might, our intellect, our resources to ensure we get there responsibly and optimistically.\N我们将倾尽全力、智慧与资源，负责任且乐观地抵达那个目标。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:25.00,1:36:25.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:25.40,1:36:29.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, there's just so many people doing the right things.\N所以，有太多人在做正确的事。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:29.07,1:36:31.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, oftentimes, you know,\N现在，经常有人，
Dialogue: 0,1:36:31.10,1:36:38.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,there there there's there there people who pontificate about these things and they're informed by several\N会就这些事高谈阔论，他们依据的是多个
Dialogue: 0,1:36:38.92,1:36:44.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,several things and they and they they don't realize that there are a lot of people,\N因素，但他们没意识到，其实有很多人，
Dialogue: 0,1:36:44.32,1:36:50.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,industries, incredible researchers and engineers outside of their sphere Mhm.\N行业、令人惊叹的研究人员和工程师，他们都在自己领域之外创造着奇迹。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:50.12,1:36:55.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,of information that are doing amazing things all by themselves independent of them.\N他们正在独立自主地做着令人惊叹的事情，完全不受外界影响。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:55.82,1:36:57.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just because they didn't say Right.\N仅仅因为他们没说“对”。
Dialogue: 0,1:36:57.88,1:37:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,they didn't say it doesn't mean a lot of smart people are doing smart things.\N他们没说，并不意味着许多聪明人没有在做聪明的事。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:00.48,1:37:00.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:01.00,1:37:06.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and you know, I say this all the time inside the company, even without my leadership,\N而且我经常在公司内部说，即使没有我的领导，
Dialogue: 0,1:37:06.42,1:37:10.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,without strategies, the company is doing smart things all by itself.\N没有战略，公司本身也在自主地做着聪明的事。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:10.56,1:37:11.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:11.12,1:37:12.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Smart people do smart things.\N聪明人会做聪明的事。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:12.95,1:37:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,They do more impactful things when you organize a line, Right.\N但当你把他们组织起来，他们能做出更有影响力的事，对吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:16.40,1:37:19.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,but amazing people are doing smart things all by themselves.\N但那些了不起的人，即使独自一人也在做聪明的事。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:19.76,1:37:24.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, when somebody tells me that that you know, you're you're worrying about It's good that we worry.\N所以，当有人告诉我，你知道，你在担心这件事，很好，我们确实该担心。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:24.84,1:37:25.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:25.24,1:37:27.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we should express our worries.\N我们应该表达我们的担忧。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:27.36,1:37:29.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We should express our concerns.\N我们应该表达我们的关切。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:29.72,1:37:32.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we shouldn't predict the end of things.\N但我们不应预言事物的终结。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:32.80,1:37:33.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:33.19,1:37:38.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because they're underestimating the human condition, they're underestimating the human capacity,\N因为他们低估了人类的处境，低估了人类的能力，
Dialogue: 0,1:37:38.26,1:37:46.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,and they think for some some reason with maybe it's just hubris, maybe it's arrogance, that unless they do it, it won't get done.\N他们认为出于某种原因，也许是傲慢，也许是自大，除非他们去做，否则事情就不会完成。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:46.92,1:37:47.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:47.33,1:37:47.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:47.74,1:37:50.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Unless they do it, it won't get done.\N除非他们去做，否则事情就不会完成。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:51.04,1:37:55.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,The fact of the matter is this company is doing amazing things whether I say it or not.\N事实是，这家公司正在做惊人的事情，无论我说不说。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:55.24,1:37:59.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, and I you know, I get I get all the accolades and the blame.\N好吧，我明白，所有的赞誉和责备我都得承受。
Dialogue: 0,1:37:59.50,1:38:03.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But um in both cases in both cases I'm fair.\N但总的来说，两种情况我都觉得公平。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:03.72,1:38:06.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm especially the accolades.\N我尤其看重这些赞誉。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:06.12,1:38:09.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so I and the reason for that is just these you know,\N而且，这就是原因所在，你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,1:38:09.22,1:38:15.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,when you surround yourself with amazing people and you create the conditions by which everybody wants the same outcome.\N当你身边聚集了优秀的人，并且创造了让每个人都渴望相同结果的环境时。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:15.88,1:38:17.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,The good the good version of it.\N那种积极的版本。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:17.37,1:38:18.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think most people do.\N我认为大多数人都是这样想的。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:18.54,1:38:24.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's the reason why I say we need to we need to hold ourselves accountable and responsible.\N这就是为什么我说我们必须对自己负责、保持问责。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:24.84,1:38:27.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we should express a future that's optimistic.\N但我们应该描绘一个乐观的未来。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:27.65,1:38:28.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,For sure.\N当然。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:28.33,1:38:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I am I am 99.99% certain that surrounded by all the amazing people in the world, we're going to get there together.\N我百分之九十九点九九确定，只要身边有全世界这么多优秀的人，我们一定能一起达成目标。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:35.64,1:38:37.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, agreed.\N是的，我同意。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:37.48,1:38:40.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's a I think you're a national treasure.\N而且我认为你真是国家的瑰宝。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:40.37,1:38:43.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're lucky to have you helping to lead the charge.\N很幸运有你来带领大家前进。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:43.60,1:38:48.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,The nation's indebted to you for getting everybody together, getting us all on the same page, building the framework.\N国家要感谢你把所有人聚在一起，让我们达成共识，搭建起框架。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:48.56,1:38:51.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's going to be more work to do.\N还有更多工作要做。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:51.40,1:38:56.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,But as a father of two and I know you you have kids, you're going to have grandkids.\N但作为两个孩子的父亲，我知道你也有孩子，将来还会有了孙辈。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:56.73,1:38:58.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't care about anything more.\N我们不再关心其他任何事。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:58.88,1:38:59.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,1:38:59.52,1:39:02.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Than actually building a better world for them, right?\N比为他们创造一个更美好的世界更重要，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:39:02.22,1:39:03.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could easily stop.\N我们完全可以停下来。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:03.48,1:39:05.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if we stop today, we lose, right?\N但如果我们今天停下，就输了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:39:05.89,1:39:08.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We lose the opportunity at that better world.\N我们将错失那个更美好世界的机遇。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:08.20,1:39:09.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we'll wrap it there.\N那我们就说到这儿。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:09.78,1:39:10.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Jensen.\N谢谢你，黄仁勋。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:10.88,1:39:11.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, guys.\N谢谢大家。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:12.02,1:39:15.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Brad, thank you for I've never met a greater patriot.\N布拉德，谢谢你，我从未见过比你更爱国的人。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:16.02,1:39:21.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Somebody who who cares so much about the industry but even more so the\N一个如此关心行业的人，但更关心的是国家。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:21.38,1:39:29.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,country and and your your gift your gift in your enthusiasm and just tireless energy.\N你那充满热情的天赋，以及永不疲倦的精力。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:29.56,1:39:38.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,In in coordinating pulling together a lot of people in order to do something great like what you did.\N在协调并召集许多人，共同完成像你所做的这样伟大的事业方面。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:38.32,1:39:48.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Incredible.\N非常了不起。
Dialogue: 0,1:39:48.44,1:39:52.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,As a reminder to everybody, just our opinions, not investment advice.\N提醒大家一下，这只是我们的观点，不是投资建议。
